  {
    "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendar/event_44825_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/silk-road-diaries-echoes-from-east-to-west-in-ville-marie/var/ri-0.l-L2"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/19_jun_CMM_jmalobaton_-13-e1725711929972.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g744740"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/organizer": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g744780"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendar/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Silk Road diaries Echoes from east to west in Ville-Marie"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>In their musical encounter, musicians <strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng) and <strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor) traverse the silk road from East to West. Their journey invites the audience along a geographical route from China via India to Italy. Together, they weave through different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200BC-9AD) to music from the emerging European 15<sup>th</sup> century Renaissance.</p> <p>The program equally imagines and draws inspirations from different physical and emotional landscapes that might be encountered by a timeless traveller – from witnessing a deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to adventurously daring to set out on a long journey, to the loneliness that a traveller can experience far away from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments, and the manifold vibrations of their strings, giving room for improvisations, and an exploration of the unknown.</p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-10-15T19:30-4::00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/endDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-10-15T20:30-4::00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
