    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Current MonthCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47296_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Renaissance Dances Workshop – April\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/renaissance-dances-workshop-april/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-4-11T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-4-11T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Atelier-Danses-Renaissance-avril.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The <strong>Renaissance</strong> was an important period for the development of <strong>dance</strong> in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.<br /> This series of <strong>workshops</strong> offered by <strong>Anne-Marie Gardette</strong> will focus on the dances of the Italian courts of the Quattrocento and Cinquecento (bassa danza, balletto, etc.). The ball repertoire in use in France at the end of the 16th century, according to Thoinot Arbeau&#8217;s essential Orchésographie (branle, pavane, gaillarde, etc.), will also be covered.</p> <p>These two-hour workshops are open to all, and musicians who play this repertoire (Praetorius, Attaingnant, Gervaise, Phalèse, etc.) and want to learn about the dances are also welcome.</p> <p>Each workshop will cover different dances, so they can be taken independently.</p> <p>Open to all.<br /> Upcoming workshops:<br /> May 2<br /> From 2:00 pm to 4:00 pm</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat11apr14 h 00 min16 h 00 minRenaissance Dances Workshop – April14 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsThe Renaissance was an important period for the development of dance in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.\nThis series of workshops offered    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The Renaissance was an important period for the development of dance in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.\nThis series of workshops offered by Anne-Marie Gardette will focus on the dances of the Italian courts of the Quattrocento and Cinquecento (bassa danza, balletto, etc.). The ball repertoire in use in France at the end of the 16th century, according to Thoinot Arbeau’s essential Orchésographie (branle, pavane, gaillarde, etc.), will also be covered.\nThese two-hour workshops are open to all, and musicians who play this repertoire (Praetorius, Attaingnant, Gervaise, Phalèse, etc.) and want to learn about the dances are also welcome.\nEach workshop will cover different dances, so they can be taken independently.\nOpen to all.\nUpcoming workshops:\nMay 2\nFrom 2:00 pm to 4:00 pm\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44583_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"The Valley of Dreams\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/the-valley-of-dreams/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-4-15T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-4-15T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CONCERT-6.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>With <em><strong>The Valley of Dreams</strong></em>, the <strong>Perse-Inca duo</strong> formed by <strong>Federico Tarazona</strong> (charango) and <strong>Showan Tavakol</strong> (kamancheh) continue the journey they began with their first album, Échos des montagnes.<br /> In this new phase, Andean and Persian strings respond to each other like two ancient voices reunited across time. True to the spirit of the initial project, the artists weave soundscapes where each note becomes a link between two worlds.</p> <p>Between improvisation, original compositions, and subtle references to tradition, this concert invites a timeless dialogue, imbued with nuances and vibrant sensations.</p> <p><strong>Artists:</strong><br /> Federico Tarazona: charango<br /> Showan Tavakol: kamancheh</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed15apr19 h 30 min20 h 30 minThe Valley of DreamsConcert intime19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT+01:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsWith The Valley of Dreams, the Perse-Inca duo formed by Federico Tarazona (charango) and Showan Tavakol (kamancheh) continue the journey they began with their first album, Échos des montagnes.\nIn    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                With The Valley of Dreams, the Perse-Inca duo formed by Federico Tarazona (charango) and Showan Tavakol (kamancheh) continue the journey they began with their first album, Échos des montagnes.\nIn this new phase, Andean and Persian strings respond to each other like two ancient voices reunited across time. True to the spirit of the initial project, the artists weave soundscapes where each note becomes a link between two worlds.\nBetween improvisation, original compositions, and subtle references to tradition, this concert invites a timeless dialogue, imbued with nuances and vibrant sensations.\nArtists:\nFederico Tarazona: charango\nShowan Tavakol: kamancheh\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeI reserve my place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47097_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"April traditional song veillée\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/april-traditional-song-veillee/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-4-24T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-4-24T22:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/273x195-veillee.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Every last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of traditional songs from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!<br /> Regulars, newcomers, and accompanying musicians are all welcome!</p> <p>The veillée is hosted by <strong>Lysandre Chartrand.</strong></p> <p>Fridays, April 24, and May 29, 2026, from 7:30 pm to 10:30 pm<br /> Cost: $10 (cash only)</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Lysandre Chartrand\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri24apr19 h 30 min22 h 30 minApril traditional song veillée19 h 30 min - 22 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsEvery last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of traditional songs from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!\nRegulars, newcomers,    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Every last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of traditional songs from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!\nRegulars, newcomers, and accompanying musicians are all welcome!\nThe veillée is hosted by Lysandre Chartrand.\nFridays, April 24, and May 29, 2026, from 7:30 pm to 10:30 pm\nCost: $10 (cash only)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47301_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Renaissance Dance Workshop – May\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/renaissance-dance-workshop-may/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-5-2T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-5-2T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Atelier-Danses-Renaissance-mai.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The <strong>Renaissance</strong> was an important period for the development of <strong>dance</strong> in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.</p> <p>This <strong>series of workshops</strong> offered by <strong>Anne-Marie Gardette</strong> will focus on the dances of the Italian courts of the Quattrocento and Cinquecento (bassa danza, balletto, etc.). The ball repertoire in use in France at the end of the 16th century, according to Thoinot Arbeau&#8217;s essential Orchésographie (branle, pavane, gaillarde, etc.), will also be covered.</p> <p>These two-hour workshops are open to all, and musicians who play this repertoire (Praetorius, Attaingnant, Gervaise, Phalèse, etc.) and want to learn about the dances are also welcome.</p> <p>Each workshop will cover different dances, so they can be taken independently.<br /> Open to all.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat02may14 h 00 min16 h 00 minRenaissance Dance Workshop – May14 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsThe Renaissance was an important period for the development of dance in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.\nThis series of workshops offered by    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The Renaissance was an important period for the development of dance in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.\nThis series of workshops offered by Anne-Marie Gardette will focus on the dances of the Italian courts of the Quattrocento and Cinquecento (bassa danza, balletto, etc.). The ball repertoire in use in France at the end of the 16th century, according to Thoinot Arbeau’s essential Orchésographie (branle, pavane, gaillarde, etc.), will also be covered.\nThese two-hour workshops are open to all, and musicians who play this repertoire (Praetorius, Attaingnant, Gervaise, Phalèse, etc.) and want to learn about the dances are also welcome.\nEach workshop will cover different dances, so they can be taken independently.\nOpen to all.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47103_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"May traditional song veillée\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/may-traditional-song-veillee/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-5-29T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-5-29T22:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/273x195-veillee.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Every last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of <strong>traditional songs</strong> from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!<br /> Regulars, newcomers, and accompanying musicians are all welcome!</p> <p>The veillée is hosted by <strong>Lysandre Chartrand</strong>.</p> <p>Friday, May 29, 2026, from 7:30 pm to 10:30 pm<br /> Cost: $10 (cash only)</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Lysandre Chartrand\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri29may19 h 30 min22 h 30 minMay traditional song veillée19 h 30 min - 22 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsEvery last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of traditional songs from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!\nRegulars, newcomers,    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Every last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of traditional songs from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!\nRegulars, newcomers, and accompanying musicians are all welcome!\nThe veillée is hosted by Lysandre Chartrand.\nFriday, May 29, 2026, from 7:30 pm to 10:30 pm\nCost: $10 (cash only)\n \n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \t\n\t\t \t\t\n\t\t \t\t\n\t\t \t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t"
