n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Chants et mélodies du Rwanda\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/chants-et-melodies-du-rwanda-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-7-18T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-7-18T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/tuxedo_image-2.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Deo Munyakazi (inanga et chant)</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu18jul18 h 00 min19 h 00 minChants et mélodies du Rwanda18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsDeo Munyakazi (inanga et chant)    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Deo Munyakazi (inanga et chant)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tThéâtre des Deux Rives30 Bd du Séminaire N, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC J3B 5J4{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_40868_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Andalusyria\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/andalusyria-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-10-3T15:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-10-3T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/CA_9811-scaled-e1726788739905.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Andalusyria brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arab traditions. Nazih Borish, based in Montreal, is a self-taught oud virtuoso that founded his own school in his hometown of Lattakia, Syria. Gabriel Evangelista, a Montrealer of Spanish origin, is a flamenco-jazz pianist. Both have developed their own musical language over the course of their careers and are committed to this artistic encounter between flamenco, jazz and Syrian music, combining their cultural and personal horizons. The result: musical poetry built on soaring improvised lines that are unique from one concert to another.</p> <p><strong>Musicians: </strong>Nazih Borish (oud), Gabriel Evangelista (piano), Hanser Santos Gomez (cajón)</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Théâtre des Deux Rives\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"30 Bd du Séminaire N, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC J3B 5J4\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu03oct15 h 30 minAndalusyria15 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Théâtre des Deux Rives\n    Event DetailsAndalusyria brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arab traditions. Nazih Borish, based in Montreal, is a self-taught oud virtuoso    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Andalusyria brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arab traditions. Nazih Borish, based in Montreal, is a self-taught oud virtuoso that founded his own school in his hometown of Lattakia, Syria. Gabriel Evangelista, a Montrealer of Spanish origin, is a flamenco-jazz pianist. Both have developed their own musical language over the course of their careers and are committed to this artistic encounter between flamenco, jazz and Syrian music, combining their cultural and personal horizons. The result: musical poetry built on soaring improvised lines that are unique from one concert to another.\nMusicians: Nazih Borish (oud), Gabriel Evangelista (piano), Hanser Santos Gomez (cajón)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationThéâtre des Deux Rives30 Bd du Séminaire N, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC J3B 5J4Other Events\n\t\t\n\tPierrefonds Cultural Centre13850 Boulevard Gouin Ouest Montréal, QC H8Z 1X7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_40616_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-3/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-10-5T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-10-5T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Pierrefonds Cultural Centre\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"13850 Boulevard Gouin Ouest Montréal, QC H8Z 1X7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat05oct19 h 30 minConstellation de cordesCAM en Tournée19 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Pierrefonds Cultural Centre\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationPierrefonds Cultural Centre13850 Boulevard Gouin Ouest Montréal, QC H8Z 1X7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_39318_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Erkan Oğur &amp; Ismail Hakkı Demircioğlu\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/erkan-ogur-ismail-hakki-demircioglu-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-10-9T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-10-9T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Creation-sans-titre-1.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The Centre for World Musicians, in partnership with Soho Concept, is pleased to present a concert by Erkan Oğur and Ismail Hakkı Demircioğlu.</p> <p>This event features two of Anatolia’s most respected musicians, both famous for their contributions to Anatolian folk music and their mastery of their instruments.</p> <p>Erkan Oğur, the inventor of the fretless guitar, is a critically acclaimed guitarist whose influence extends beyond international boundaries. His collaboration with Ismail Hakkı Demircioğlu, a master of the strings, was praised for his artistic alchemy and deeply emotional performances. The duo’s repertoire includes a mix of old and new Anatolian folk songs, described as &#8220;a common attempt to recall&#8221; the soulful melodies of their homeland.</p> <p>For more than twenty years, Oğur and Demircioğlu have been breathing new life into the songs of Anatolia, mixing traditional instruments like saz and bağlama lute with modern fretless guitar sounds. Their collaborations have resulted in several albums and concerts acclaimed around the world, drawing on musical traditions that date back to the 14th century.</p> <p>This concert at the Saint-Enfant-Jésus church in Mile-End offers a rare opportunity to discover the depth and beauty of Anatolian folk music, performed by two of its most authentic and competent practitioners. Don’t miss this opportunity to attend a live performance that promises to be a sincere tribute to the rich musical heritage of Anatolia.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed09oct20 h 00 minErkan Oğur & Ismail Hakkı Demircioğlu20 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsThe Centre for World Musicians, in partnership with Soho Concept, is pleased to present a concert by Erkan Oğur and Ismail Hakkı Demircioğlu.\nThis event features two of Anatolia’s most respected    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The Centre for World Musicians, in partnership with Soho Concept, is pleased to present a concert by Erkan Oğur and Ismail Hakkı Demircioğlu.\nThis event features two of Anatolia’s most respected musicians, both famous for their contributions to Anatolian folk music and their mastery of their instruments.\nErkan Oğur, the inventor of the fretless guitar, is a critically acclaimed guitarist whose influence extends beyond international boundaries. His collaboration with Ismail Hakkı Demircioğlu, a master of the strings, was praised for his artistic alchemy and deeply emotional performances. The duo’s repertoire includes a mix of old and new Anatolian folk songs, described as “a common attempt to recall” the soulful melodies of their homeland.\nFor more than twenty years, Oğur and Demircioğlu have been breathing new life into the songs of Anatolia, mixing traditional instruments like saz and bağlama lute with modern fretless guitar sounds. Their collaborations have resulted in several albums and concerts acclaimed around the world, drawing on musical traditions that date back to the 14th century.\nThis concert at the Saint-Enfant-Jésus church in Mile-End offers a rare opportunity to discover the depth and beauty of Anatolian folk music, performed by two of its most authentic and competent practitioners. Don’t miss this opportunity to attend a live performance that promises to be a sincere tribute to the rich musical heritage of Anatolia.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_40899_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Fundraising evening\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/fundraising-evening/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-10-10T18:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-10-10T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/thumbnail_Traversees-4-©-Federico-Cavicchioli-2-scaled-e1726258281266.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<section class='av_textblock_section av-m115sejx-d013ec4a76fd67c6775850dd85c93424 '> <div class='avia_textblock'> <p>We invite you to a <strong>unique evening</strong>, designed to delight your taste buds, your ears and your eyes. This opportunity to support the mission of the Centre des musiciens du monde is an experience <strong>open exclusively</strong> to 50 people to encourage the tasting of atmospheres, music and flavours from around the world.</p> <p>In the first part of the evening, you can wander around discovering instruments, sounds and wisdom from the world. Then, we offer you an intimate concert offered by two internationally renowned artists: <strong>Ablaye Cissoko</strong>, one of the greatest representatives of the kora in Africa and <strong>Kiya Tabassian</strong>, a setar virtuoso from Iran who will lead you on the paths of musical dialogue, friendship beyond borders and generous sharing.</p> </div> </section> <div class='hr av-1pixnyz-e76f70f08837d389457e85f6bed5c857 hr-invisible avia-builder-el-8 el_after_av_textblock el_before_av_textblock '></div> <section class='av_textblock_section av-m115sm1x-be757e468bcbbdc63075ee79158d6afd '> <div class='avia_textblock'> <p><u>An evening limited to 50 people</u></p> <p>6:30 p.m.: Cocktail dinner ~ World explorations</p> <p>8 p.m.: Intimate concert (unique in Canada)</p> </div> </section> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu10oct18 h 30 minFundraising eveningAblaye Cissoko & Kiya Tabassian18 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsWe invite you to a unique evening, designed to delight your taste buds, your ears and your eyes. This opportunity to support the mission of the Centre    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                \n\nWe invite you to a unique evening, designed to delight your taste buds, your ears and your eyes. This opportunity to support the mission of the Centre des musiciens du monde is an experience open exclusively to 50 people to encourage the tasting of atmospheres, music and flavours from around the world.\nIn the first part of the evening, you can wander around discovering instruments, sounds and wisdom from the world. Then, we offer you an intimate concert offered by two internationally renowned artists: Ablaye Cissoko, one of the greatest representatives of the kora in Africa and Kiya Tabassian, a setar virtuoso from Iran who will lead you on the paths of musical dialogue, friendship beyond borders and generous sharing.\n\n\n\n\n\nAn evening limited to 50 people\n6:30 p.m.: Cocktail dinner ~ World explorations\n8 p.m.: Intimate concert (unique in Canada)\n\n\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeBuy your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_39718_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Intimate concert | Windborne\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/windborne/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-10-23T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-10-23T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Red-Bold-Modern-Music-Event-Announcement-Instagram-Post-695-x-380-px.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>“The most exciting vocal group of its generation”</strong></p> <p>Windborne&#8217;s captivating show draws on the singers&#8217; deep roots in vocal harmony traditions, while the absolute uniqueness of their artistic approach brings old songs into the present. Known for the innovation of their arrangements, their harmonies are bold and anything but predictable.</p> <p>With 20 years of experience studying polyphonic music around the world, Lauren Breunig, Jeremy Carter-Gordon, Lynn Rowan and Will Rowan share a vibrant energy on stage, with a blend of voices that could only come from decades of friendship and diligent practice. The ensemble moves effortlessly from one style of music to another, taking the audience on a journey that spans continents and centuries, illuminating and expanding the profound power and variety of the human voice. Singers educate while entertaining, sharing stories about their songs and explaining the context and characteristics of the styles in which they sing.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed23oct20 h 00 minIntimate concert | Windborne20 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event Details“The most exciting vocal group of its generation”\nWindborne’s captivating show draws on the singers’ deep roots in vocal harmony traditions, while the absolute uniqueness of their artistic approach brings old    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                “The most exciting vocal group of its generation”\nWindborne’s captivating show draws on the singers’ deep roots in vocal harmony traditions, while the absolute uniqueness of their artistic approach brings old songs into the present. Known for the innovation of their arrangements, their harmonies are bold and anything but predictable.\nWith 20 years of experience studying polyphonic music around the world, Lauren Breunig, Jeremy Carter-Gordon, Lynn Rowan and Will Rowan share a vibrant energy on stage, with a blend of voices that could only come from decades of friendship and diligent practice. The ensemble moves effortlessly from one style of music to another, taking the audience on a journey that spans continents and centuries, illuminating and expanding the profound power and variety of the human voice. Singers educate while entertaining, sharing stories about their songs and explaining the context and characteristics of the styles in which they sing.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeBuy ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture Marie-Uguay6052 Bd Monk, Montréal, QC H4E 3H6{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_40628_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-5/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-10-26T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-10-26T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture Marie-Uguay\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"6052 Bd Monk, Montréal, QC H4E 3H6\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat26oct14 h 00 minConstellation de cordesCAM en Tournée14 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Maison de la culture Marie-Uguay\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture Marie-Uguay6052 Bd Monk, Montréal, QC H4E 3H6Other Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre Culturel St-John593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, Canada{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_40870_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Quartette\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-quartette-3/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-11-16T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-11-16T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC_4021@prodKastallis-scaled-e1726693008557.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Music that makes you travel! With the sounds of jazz, the subtleties of classical, the klezmer inflections and the tango rhythms.</p> <p>Renowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity, the four musicians present Villes Éternelles, in which the long and rich tradition of oriental music permeates each of Masmoudi&#8217;s compositions with its modes (maqamat) and metrics.</p> <p>Masmoudi&#8217;s original compositions are permeated by the rich oriental sounds of the oud, with classical and jazz accents from Eastern Europe, complemented by piano, double bass and clarinet. A host of influences raked together along the way, in a truly open and experimental approach.</p> <p>With: Guillaume Martineau on piano, Rémi-Jean Leblanc on double bass, Gabriel Paquin-Buki on guitar and Mohamed Masmoudi on clarinet.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre Culturel St-John\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, Canada\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat16nov15 h 00 minMasmoudi Quartette15 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre Culturel St-John\n    Event DetailsMusic that makes you travel! With the sounds of jazz, the subtleties of classical, the klezmer inflections and the tango rhythms.\nRenowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity, the four musicians    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Music that makes you travel! With the sounds of jazz, the subtleties of classical, the klezmer inflections and the tango rhythms.\nRenowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity, the four musicians present Villes Éternelles, in which the long and rich tradition of oriental music permeates each of Masmoudi’s compositions with its modes (maqamat) and metrics.\nMasmoudi’s original compositions are permeated by the rich oriental sounds of the oud, with classical and jazz accents from Eastern Europe, complemented by piano, double bass and clarinet. A host of influences raked together along the way, in a truly open and experimental approach.\nWith: Guillaume Martineau on piano, Rémi-Jean Leblanc on double bass, Gabriel Paquin-Buki on guitar and Mohamed Masmoudi on clarinet.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeRéservez votre place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre Culturel St-John593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, CanadaOther Events\n\t\t\n\tThéâtre Alphonse-Desjardins25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_40878_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-11-16T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-11-16T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat16nov20 h 00 minConstellation de cordesCAM en Tournée20 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationThéâtre Alphonse-Desjardins25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2Other Events\n\t\t\n\tÉglise Saint-René-Goupil4251 Rue du Parc-René-Goupil Montréal, QC H1Z 1X8{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41316_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-7/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-11-17T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-11-17T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Église Saint-René-Goupil\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"4251 Rue du Parc-René-Goupil Montréal, QC H1Z 1X8\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun17nov16 h 00 minConstellation de cordesCAM en Tournée16 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Église Saint-René-Goupil\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationÉglise Saint-René-Goupil4251 Rue du Parc-René-Goupil Montréal, QC H1Z 1X8Other Events\n\t\t\n\tEspace Jax1439 rue Sainte-Catherine Ouest, Montreal QC H3G 1S6{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41327_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-10/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-11-18T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-11-18T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Espace Jax\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"1439 rue Sainte-Catherine Ouest, Montreal QC H3G 1S6\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tmon18nov20 h 00 minConstellation de cordes20 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Espace Jax\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationEspace Jax1439 rue Sainte-Catherine Ouest, Montreal QC H3G 1S6Other Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges5290 Chemin de la Côte-des-Neiges Montréal, QC H3T 1Y2{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41579_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-12/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-11-19T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-11-19T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5290 Chemin de la Côte-des-Neiges Montréal, QC H3T 1Y2\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\ttue19nov19 h 30 minConstellation de cordesCAM en Tournée19 h 30 min(GMT-05:00) Maison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges5290 Chemin de la Côte-des-Neiges Montréal, QC H3T 1Y2Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41249_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"The CMM showcase: triple program\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/the-cmm-showcase-triple-program/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-11-22T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-11-22T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/OFF_Banniere-spectacle_2024_STORY_OFF_1080X1920_22NOV.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>As part of the Mundial Montréal conference event, the Centre des musiciens du monde is showcasing three works that combine sounds and instruments from Mongolia, Iran, Peru, Mali, and Brazil.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Carnets de soie &#8211; from Persia to Mongolia</strong></p> <p>On the musical paths joining the Silk Road, Uuriintuya Khalivan, carrying the breath of Mongolia, and Sadaf Amini, the echoes of Iran, met in Montreal. Together, they trace their itinerary, where each note becomes a pause on discovering the Other. They celebrate the richness of their respective cultures, woven like silk threads, seeking harmonies beyond borders, beyond distances.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Duo Perse-Inca</strong></p> <p>Duo Perse-Inca is the fruit of a meeting in Montreal between a Peruvian and an Iranian musician, both bearers of the rich traditions of Iran: Showan Tavakol on kamancheh fiddle, and Federico Tarazona on charango guitar. This collaboration has brought together ancient musical systems, which the two artists explore through the delicacy of Andean melodies and the depth of Persian music. By marrying languages, techniques and aesthetics, they give birth to a music that is both ancient in its roots and modern through this unexpected encounter.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Siraba &#8211; Adama Daou</strong></p> <p>Siraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents&#8230;</p> <p>This is the name of our latest show, an artistic dialogue between the emblematic languages of West Africa, South America and Europe, based on Mali&#8217;s 12-blade balafon and Manding guitar (Aboulayé Koné), Brazil&#8217;s pandeiro and saxophone (Gabriel Schwartz) and double bass (Olivier Babaz). A refreshingly syncopated encounter, where ancient traditions are renewed through a dialogue that opens up a new universe of great beauty.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>***</p> <p><strong>Showcase schedule:</strong></p> <p>19:00 &#8211; Doors open</p> <p>20:00 &#8211; Carnets de soie &#8211; from Persia to Mongolia</p> <p>20:30 &#8211; Persian-Inca Duo</p> <p>21:00 &#8211; Siraba &#8211; Adama Daou</p> <p>***</p> <p><strong>Free for Mundial Montréal PRO and DÉCOUVERTE badge holders</strong></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri22nov20 h 00 minThe CMM showcase: triple programOff-Mundial Montréal20 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsAs part of the Mundial Montréal conference event, the Centre des musiciens du monde is showcasing three works that combine sounds and instruments from Mongolia, Iran, Peru, Mali, and Brazil.\n \nCarnets    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                As part of the Mundial Montréal conference event, the Centre des musiciens du monde is showcasing three works that combine sounds and instruments from Mongolia, Iran, Peru, Mali, and Brazil.\n \nCarnets de soie – from Persia to Mongolia\nOn the musical paths joining the Silk Road, Uuriintuya Khalivan, carrying the breath of Mongolia, and Sadaf Amini, the echoes of Iran, met in Montreal. Together, they trace their itinerary, where each note becomes a pause on discovering the Other. They celebrate the richness of their respective cultures, woven like silk threads, seeking harmonies beyond borders, beyond distances.\n \nDuo Perse-Inca\nDuo Perse-Inca is the fruit of a meeting in Montreal between a Peruvian and an Iranian musician, both bearers of the rich traditions of Iran: Showan Tavakol on kamancheh fiddle, and Federico Tarazona on charango guitar. This collaboration has brought together ancient musical systems, which the two artists explore through the delicacy of Andean melodies and the depth of Persian music. By marrying languages, techniques and aesthetics, they give birth to a music that is both ancient in its roots and modern through this unexpected encounter.\n \n \nSiraba – Adama Daou\nSiraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nThis is the name of our latest show, an artistic dialogue between the emblematic languages of West Africa, South America and Europe, based on Mali’s 12-blade balafon and Manding guitar (Aboulayé Koné), Brazil’s pandeiro and saxophone (Gabriel Schwartz) and double bass (Olivier Babaz). A refreshingly syncopated encounter, where ancient traditions are renewed through a dialogue that opens up a new universe of great beauty.\n \n***\nShowcase schedule:\n19:00 – Doors open\n20:00 – Carnets de soie – from Persia to Mongolia\n20:30 – Persian-Inca Duo\n21:00 – Siraba – Adama Daou\n***\nFree for Mundial Montréal PRO and DÉCOUVERTE badge holders\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture Janine-Sutto2550 Rue Ontario Est Montréal, QC H2K 1W7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41592_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-14/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-11-28T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-11-28T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture Janine-Sutto\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"2550 Rue Ontario Est Montréal, QC H2K 1W7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu28nov19 h 00 minConstellation de cordes19 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Maison de la culture Janine-Sutto\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture Janine-Sutto2550 Rue Ontario Est Montréal, QC H2K 1W7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSarto-Desnoyers Community Centre1335 chemin du Bord-du-Lac—Lakeshore Dorval, Québec H9S 2E5{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41599_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-16/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-12-1T11:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-12-1T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Sarto-Desnoyers Community Centre\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"1335 chemin du Bord-du-Lac—Lakeshore Dorval, Québec H9S 2E5\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun01dec11 h 00 minConstellation de cordes11 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Sarto-Desnoyers Community Centre\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSarto-Desnoyers Community Centre1335 chemin du Bord-du-Lac—Lakeshore Dorval, Québec H9S 2E5Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41352_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Chants d&#039;espoir Kayhan Kalhor\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/chants-despoir-kayhan-kalhor-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2024-12-16T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2024-12-16T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/media_imaga_principal_tuxedo.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>6:15 p.m.: doors open and access to the refreshment bar<br /> 6:30 p.m.-7 p.m.: Pre-concert meeting with Kiya Tabassian (hosted by Frédéric Léotar, ethnomusicologist)<br /> 8 p.m.: concert</p> <p>One of Iran’s most beloved artists and the preeminent ambassador of Persian music, Kayhan Kalhor  is a soulful master of the  kamancheh, the Persian spiked fiddle. Widely known for his stirring improvisations, exquisite compositions, and extensive collaborations, Kalhor returns to Vancouver alongside setar virtuoso Kiya Tabassian, and one of the greatest voices of new generation Iran’s singers, Hadi Hosseini. Together, they will present a unique sublime Persian music and poetry program.</p> <p>Distribution :</p> <p>KAYHAN KALHOR, kamancheh</p> <p>HADI HOSSEINI, vocals</p> <p>KIYA TABASIAN, setar</p> <p>HAMIN HONARI, tombak</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tmon16dec20 h 00 minChants d'espoir Kayhan Kalhor20 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event Details6:15 p.m.: doors open and access to the refreshment bar\n6:30 p.m.-7 p.m.: Pre-concert meeting with Kiya Tabassian (hosted by Frédéric Léotar, ethnomusicologist)\n8 p.m.: concert\nOne of Iran’s most beloved    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                6:15 p.m.: doors open and access to the refreshment bar\n6:30 p.m.-7 p.m.: Pre-concert meeting with Kiya Tabassian (hosted by Frédéric Léotar, ethnomusicologist)\n8 p.m.: concert\nOne of Iran’s most beloved artists and the preeminent ambassador of Persian music, Kayhan Kalhor  is a soulful master of the  kamancheh, the Persian spiked fiddle. Widely known for his stirring improvisations, exquisite compositions, and extensive collaborations, Kalhor returns to Vancouver alongside setar virtuoso Kiya Tabassian, and one of the greatest voices of new generation Iran’s singers, Hadi Hosseini. Together, they will present a unique sublime Persian music and poetry program.\nDistribution :\nKAYHAN KALHOR, kamancheh\nHADI HOSSEINI, vocals\nKIYA TABASIAN, setar\nHAMIN HONARI, tombak\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41806_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Ender Balkir\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/ender-balkir-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-1-19T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-1-19T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/concert-19-janvier.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<div class='xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs'><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t9e/1/16/1f3b5.png' alt='🎵' width='16' height='16' /></span> Ender Balkır Live in Montreal <span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t9e/1/16/1f3b5.png' alt='🎵' width='16' height='16' /></span></div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Join us for an unforgettable evening of music and culture with the renowned folk artist Ender Balkır! Known for his mesmerizing voice and masterful interpretations of Anatolian folk songs.</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Co-produced by the Centre for Musicians of the World and Soro-production, this event will occur at the Saint-Enfant-Jésus du Mile End Church from 7:30 PM to 10:30 PM. A refreshment bar will be available, and there will be an intermission.</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t7e/1/16/1f4c5.png' alt='📅' width='16' height='16' /></span> Date: Sunday, January 19, 2025<br class='html-br' /><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t34/1/16/23f0.png' alt='⏰' width='16' height='16' /></span> Time: 8:00 PM – 10:00 PM (Doors open at 7:15 PM)<br class='html-br' /><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t2d/1/16/1f4cd.png' alt='📍' width='16' height='16' /></span> Location: Saint-Enfant-Jesus church in Mile End, 5039 Saint-Dominique street, Montreal, QC H2T 1V1</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Prepare for an evening filled with soulful melodies that transcend borders, celebrating the rich heritage of folk music. Don’t miss this unique opportunity to experience a live performance by one of the most celebrated voices.</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/td8/1/16/1f39f.png' alt='🎟️' width='16' height='16' /></span> Reserve your spot now and be part of an enchanting musical journey.</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>________________________________________</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t9e/1/16/1f3b5.png' alt='🎵' width='16' height='16' /></span> Ender Balkır Montreal’da! <span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t9e/1/16/1f3b5.png' alt='🎵' width='16' height='16' /></span></div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Ünlü halk müziği sanatçısı Ender Balkır ile müzik ve kültür dolu unutulmaz bir akşama davetlisiniz! Anadolu’nun zengin halk ezgilerini büyüleyici sesiyle yorumlayan Ender Balkır.</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t7e/1/16/1f4c5.png' alt='📅' width='16' height='16' /></span> Tarih: Pazar, 19 Ocak 2025<br class='html-br' /><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t34/1/16/23f0.png' alt='⏰' width='16' height='16' /></span> Saat: 20:00 &#8211; 22:00 (Kapılar 19:15&#8217;te açılır)<br class='html-br' /><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/t2d/1/16/1f4cd.png' alt='📍' width='16' height='16' /></span> Yer: Saint-Enfant-Jesus church in Mile End, 5039 Saint-Dominique street, Montreal, QC H2T 1V1</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>halk müziğinin zengin mirasını kutlayan ve sınırları aşan ezgilerle dolu bir geceye hazır olun.</div> <div class='x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'><span class='html-span xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x1hl2dhg x16tdsg8 x1vvkbs x3nfvp2 x1j61x8r x1fcty0u xdj266r xat24cr xgzva0m xhhsvwb xxymvpz xlup9mm x1kky2od'><img class='xz74otr' src='https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/images/emoji.php/v9/td8/1/16/1f39f.png' alt='🎟️' width='16' height='16' /></span> Hemen yerinizi ayırtın ve büyüleyici bir müzik yolculuğuna katılın.</div> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun19jan20 h 00 minEnder Balkir20 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event Details Ender    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                 Ender Balkır Live in Montreal \nJoin us for an unforgettable evening of music and culture with the renowned folk artist Ender Balkır! Known for his mesmerizing voice and masterful interpretations of Anatolian folk songs.\nCo-produced by the Centre for Musicians of the World and Soro-production, this event will occur at the Saint-Enfant-Jésus du Mile End Church from 7:30 PM to 10:30 PM. A refreshment bar will be available, and there will be an intermission.\n Date: Sunday, January 19, 2025 Time: 8:00 PM – 10:00 PM (Doors open at 7:15 PM) Location: Saint-Enfant-Jesus church in Mile End, 5039 Saint-Dominique street, Montreal, QC H2T 1V1\nPrepare for an evening filled with soulful melodies that transcend borders, celebrating the rich heritage of folk music. Don’t miss this unique opportunity to experience a live performance by one of the most celebrated voices.\n Reserve your spot now and be part of an enchanting musical journey.\n________________________________________\n Ender Balkır Montreal’da! \nÜnlü halk müziği sanatçısı Ender Balkır ile müzik ve kültür dolu unutulmaz bir akşama davetlisiniz! Anadolu’nun zengin halk ezgilerini büyüleyici sesiyle yorumlayan Ender Balkır.\n Tarih: Pazar, 19 Ocak 2025 Saat: 20:00 – 22:00 (Kapılar 19:15’te açılır) Yer: Saint-Enfant-Jesus church in Mile End, 5039 Saint-Dominique street, Montreal, QC H2T 1V1\nhalk müziğinin zengin mirasını kutlayan ve sınırları aşan ezgilerle dolu bir geceye hazır olun.\n Hemen yerinizi ayırtın ve büyüleyici bir müzik yolculuğuna katılın.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSt-Jax Center1439, rue Sainte-Catherine Ouest Montréal (Québec) H3G 1S6{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41820_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Carnets de soie: echoes from east to west\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/carnets-de-soie-echoes-from-east-to-west/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-1-25T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-1-25T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-14-2-scaled-e1726260009258.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The program is inspired by different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveller might encounter &#8211; from the observation of deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveller might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between their instruments&#8217; sounds and their strings&#8217; multiple vibrations, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.</p> <p>The audience is invited to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, weaving in links between different historical periods and presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC &#8211; 9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor)</p> <p><strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng)</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"St-Jax Center\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"1439, rue Sainte-Catherine Ouest Montréal (Québec) H3G 1S6\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat25jan20 h 00 minCarnets de soie: echoes from east to west20 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) St-Jax Center\n    Event DetailsThe program is inspired by different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveller might encounter – from the observation of deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to the audacity    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The program is inspired by different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveller might encounter – from the observation of deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveller might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between their instruments’ sounds and their strings’ multiple vibrations, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.\nThe audience is invited to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, weaving in links between different historical periods and presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC – 9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.\n \nAnnette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor)\nRan Wang (guzheng)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSt-Jax Center1439, rue Sainte-Catherine Ouest Montréal (Québec) H3G 1S6Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLe Carré 150150, rue Notre-Dame Est, Victoriaville, G6P 3Z6{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41809_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Quartette\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-quartette-6/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-1-26T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-1-26T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC_4021@prodKastallis-scaled-e1726693008557.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Music that makes you travel! With the sounds of jazz, the subtleties of classical, the klezmer inflections and the tango rhythms.</p> <p>Renowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity, the four musicians present Villes Éternelles, in which the long and rich tradition of oriental music permeates each of Masmoudi&#8217;s compositions with its modes (maqamat) and metrics.</p> <p>Masmoudi&#8217;s original compositions are permeated by the rich oriental sounds of the oud, with classical and jazz accents from Eastern Europe, complemented by piano, double bass and clarinet. A host of influences raked together along the way, in a truly open and experimental approach.</p> <p>With: Guillaume Martineau on piano, Rémi-Jean Leblanc on double bass, Gabriel Paquin-Buki on clarinet and Mohamed Masmoudi on oud</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Le Carré 150\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"150, rue Notre-Dame Est, Victoriaville, G6P 3Z6\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun26jan15 h 00 minMasmoudi Quartette15 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Le Carré 150\n    Event DetailsMusic that makes you travel! With the sounds of jazz, the subtleties of classical, the klezmer inflections and the tango rhythms.\nRenowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity, the four musicians    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Music that makes you travel! With the sounds of jazz, the subtleties of classical, the klezmer inflections and the tango rhythms.\nRenowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity, the four musicians present Villes Éternelles, in which the long and rich tradition of oriental music permeates each of Masmoudi’s compositions with its modes (maqamat) and metrics.\nMasmoudi’s original compositions are permeated by the rich oriental sounds of the oud, with classical and jazz accents from Eastern Europe, complemented by piano, double bass and clarinet. A host of influences raked together along the way, in a truly open and experimental approach.\nWith: Guillaume Martineau on piano, Rémi-Jean Leblanc on double bass, Gabriel Paquin-Buki on clarinet and Mohamed Masmoudi on oud\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLe Carré 150150, rue Notre-Dame Est, Victoriaville, G6P 3Z6Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41894_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Deo Munyakazi - Inanga from Rwanda\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/deo-munyakazi-inanga-from-rwanda/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-1-29T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-1-29T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/munyakazi-deo.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Deo Munyakazi is a renowned Rwandan musician, famous for his mastery of the <b>inanga</b>, a traditional harp from the African Great Lakes region. This essential instrument in Rwandan music is used to tell stories and pass on cultural values.</p> <p>Deo is committed to preserving this heritage while modernizing it. His performances, both technical and sensitive, captivate audiences, reflecting the unknown beauty of Rwandan culture. As a musical ambassador, he values oral traditions while building bridges with other styles.</p> <p>An unmissable artist for discovering the rich soundscape of Rwanda through the presentation of new traditional melodies by Deo.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed29jan20 h 00 minDeo Munyakazi - Inanga from RwandaConcert intime20 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsDeo Munyakazi is a renowned Rwandan musician, famous for his mastery of the inanga, a traditional harp from the African Great Lakes region. This essential instrument in Rwandan music is used    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Deo Munyakazi is a renowned Rwandan musician, famous for his mastery of the inanga, a traditional harp from the African Great Lakes region. This essential instrument in Rwandan music is used to tell stories and pass on cultural values.\nDeo is committed to preserving this heritage while modernizing it. His performances, both technical and sensitive, captivate audiences, reflecting the unknown beauty of Rwandan culture. As a musical ambassador, he values oral traditions while building bridges with other styles.\nAn unmissable artist for discovering the rich soundscape of Rwanda through the presentation of new traditional melodies by Deo.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture Claude-Léveillée911, rue Jean-Talon Est Montréal (Québec) H2R 1V5{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42264_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Siraba - Adama Daou\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/siraba-adama-daou-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-2-6T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-2-6T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC05501-ok-scaled-e1727542336632.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>It’s also the name of Adama Daou’s latest show, an artistic dialogue between the emblematic languages of West Africa, South America and Europe, using the balafon and Mandinka guitar (Aboulayé Koné), Brazil’s pandeiro and the saxophone (Gabriel Schwartz) and the double bass (Olivier Babaz). It is a refreshing and dynamic encounter, where a dialogue renews ancient traditions and opens a new universe of great beauty.</p> <p>Adama Daou is a musician from Mali, considered one of the greatest specialists of the balafon, the emblematic 12-blade percussion of the whole West Africa. His migration path, which took him to Quebec via France, opened the door to numerous artistic collaborations with tradition-bearers from various musical cultures. Adama Daou is a true ambassador of balafon and Mandinka culture.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture Claude-Léveillée\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"911, rue Jean-Talon Est Montréal (Québec) H2R 1V5\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu06feb19 h 30 minSiraba - Adama Daou19 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Maison de la culture Claude-Léveillée\n    Event DetailsIt’s also the name of Adama Daou’s latest show, an artistic dialogue between the emblematic languages of West Africa, South America and Europe, using the balafon and Mandinka guitar (Aboulayé    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                It’s also the name of Adama Daou’s latest show, an artistic dialogue between the emblematic languages of West Africa, South America and Europe, using the balafon and Mandinka guitar (Aboulayé Koné), Brazil’s pandeiro and the saxophone (Gabriel Schwartz) and the double bass (Olivier Babaz). It is a refreshing and dynamic encounter, where a dialogue renews ancient traditions and opens a new universe of great beauty.\nAdama Daou is a musician from Mali, considered one of the greatest specialists of the balafon, the emblematic 12-blade percussion of the whole West Africa. His migration path, which took him to Quebec via France, opened the door to numerous artistic collaborations with tradition-bearers from various musical cultures. Adama Daou is a true ambassador of balafon and Mandinka culture.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture Claude-Léveillée911, rue Jean-Talon Est Montréal (Québec) H2R 1V5Other Events\n\t\t\n\tThéâtre Alphonse-Desjardins25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42271_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Quartette\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-quartette-8/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-2-8T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-2-8T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC_4021@prodKastallis-scaled-e1726693008557.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The four musicians of the Masmoudi Quartet, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long and rich tradition of oriental music imbues each of Mohammed Masmoudi&#8217;s compositions with its own modes and metrics, on Saturday February 8 at the Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins in Repentigny (8 p.m.).</p> <p>With improvisations borrowing from jazz and classical idioms, sprinkled with klezmer inflections and tango rhythms, the works of the Masmoudi Quartet bear witness to the richness of a life begun in Tunisia and continued an ocean away, with a host of influences raked up along the way, in a truly open and experimental approach.</p> <p>For Mohamed Masmoudi, Villes Éternelles (2023) is the crystallization of several decades of creativity, work, learning and musical exchange. It is the culmination of rigorous refinements and explorations of richly diversified fields, which are inevitably linked by an Ariadne&#8217;s thread to the oud&#8217;s deep roots. The demonstration of its various uses helps us to see this instrument as more than the reflection of a distant culture, but rather the vehicle of a shared sensibility. Nominated for ADISQ and Folk Music AWARD.</p> <p>Mohamed Masmoudi &#8211; oud<br /> Gabriel Paquin-Buki &#8211; clarinet<br /> Guillaume Martineau &#8211; piano<br /> Rémi-Jean LeBlanc &#8211; double bass</p> <p>Presented by Aramusique as part of the Musique du monde series.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat08feb20 h 00 minMasmoudi Quartetteformule cabaret20 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins\n    Event DetailsThe four musicians of the Masmoudi Quartet, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The four musicians of the Masmoudi Quartet, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long and rich tradition of oriental music imbues each of Mohammed Masmoudi’s compositions with its own modes and metrics, on Saturday February 8 at the Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins in Repentigny (8 p.m.).\nWith improvisations borrowing from jazz and classical idioms, sprinkled with klezmer inflections and tango rhythms, the works of the Masmoudi Quartet bear witness to the richness of a life begun in Tunisia and continued an ocean away, with a host of influences raked up along the way, in a truly open and experimental approach.\nFor Mohamed Masmoudi, Villes Éternelles (2023) is the crystallization of several decades of creativity, work, learning and musical exchange. It is the culmination of rigorous refinements and explorations of richly diversified fields, which are inevitably linked by an Ariadne’s thread to the oud’s deep roots. The demonstration of its various uses helps us to see this instrument as more than the reflection of a distant culture, but rather the vehicle of a shared sensibility. Nominated for ADISQ and Folk Music AWARD.\nMohamed Masmoudi – oud\nGabriel Paquin-Buki – clarinet\nGuillaume Martineau – piano\nRémi-Jean LeBlanc – double bass\nPresented by Aramusique as part of the Musique du monde series.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationThéâtre Alphonse-Desjardins25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41920_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Uuriintuya Khalivan - Morinkhuur from Mongolia\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/uuriintuya-khalivan-morinkhuur-from-mongolia/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-2-12T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-2-12T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-28-scaled-e1726263500479.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Discover the fascinating beauty of the <b>morinkhuur</b>, the traditional horse-head fiddle, in the hands of Uuriintuya Khalivan, a young virtuoso from Inner Mongolia. Born into an ancient tradition, Uurintuya received her first instrument at the age of 12, a gift from her poet father.</p> <p>With her subtle playing of harmonics, the <b>morinkhuur</b> evokes the wild nature: the breath of the wind, the gallop of horses, the vastness of the steppe, and the whisper of spirits, with each note weaving a deep connection between humans and their environment.</p> <p>Let yourself be transported by the breath of this millennial music, where tradition and emotion become one. An unforgettable evening to connect with the vast Mongolian landscapes.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed12feb20 h 00 minUuriintuya Khalivan - Morinkhuur from MongoliaConcert intime20 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsDiscover the fascinating beauty of the morinkhuur, the traditional horse-head fiddle, in the hands of Uuriintuya Khalivan, a young virtuoso from Inner Mongolia. Born into an ancient tradition, Uurintuya received her    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Discover the fascinating beauty of the morinkhuur, the traditional horse-head fiddle, in the hands of Uuriintuya Khalivan, a young virtuoso from Inner Mongolia. Born into an ancient tradition, Uurintuya received her first instrument at the age of 12, a gift from her poet father.\nWith her subtle playing of harmonics, the morinkhuur evokes the wild nature: the breath of the wind, the gallop of horses, the vastness of the steppe, and the whisper of spirits, with each note weaving a deep connection between humans and their environment.\nLet yourself be transported by the breath of this millennial music, where tradition and emotion become one. An unforgettable evening to connect with the vast Mongolian landscapes.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la Culture Notre-Dame-De-Grâce3755, Botrel street H4A 3G8 Montreal{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42277_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Carnets de soie: echoes from east to west\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/carnets-de-soie-echoes-from-east-to-west-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-2-16T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-2-16T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-14-2-scaled-e1726260009258.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The program is inspired by different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveller might encounter &#8211; from the observation of deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveller might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between their instruments&#8217; sounds and their strings&#8217; multiple vibrations, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.</p> <p>The audience is invited to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, weaving in links between different historical periods and presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC &#8211; 9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor)</p> <p><strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng)</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la Culture Notre-Dame-De-Grâce\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"3755, Botrel street H4A 3G8 Montreal\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun16feb15 h 00 minCarnets de soie: echoes from east to west15 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Maison de la Culture Notre-Dame-De-Grâce\n    Event DetailsThe program is inspired by different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveller might encounter – from the observation of deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to the audacity    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The program is inspired by different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveller might encounter – from the observation of deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveller might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between their instruments’ sounds and their strings’ multiple vibrations, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.\nThe audience is invited to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, weaving in links between different historical periods and presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC – 9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.\n \nAnnette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor)\nRan Wang (guzheng)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la Culture Notre-Dame-De-Grâce3755, Botrel street H4A 3G8 MontrealOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41956_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Mig&#039;maq / Basques - From one land to another\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/migmaq-basques-from-one-land-to-another/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-3-1T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-3-1T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Sans-titre-2-scaled.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The Centre des musiciens du monde presents an unusual encounter between the musical culture of the Basque Country and that of the indigenous Mig&#8217;maq nation. The fruit of a creative residency bringing together artists from these two worlds (Darlène Gijuminag, Claudine Arhancet and Michel Etxekopar), this meeting defies borders and brings together cultures that are brothers by land.<br /> Revealing both their age-old traditions and the modernity that emanates from their recent collaborations, this concert will be punctuated by the encounter of traditional Mig&#8217;maq and Basque music, echoing the traces and faded images of their first encounters. The artists explore both real and imaginary territories, reminding us that the two communities crossed paths centuries ago.</p> <p><strong>This concert is presented in co-production with the SMCQ as part of the Montreal/New Music Festival with the participation of the Basques du Québec Euskaldunak association.</strong></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat01mar19 h 30 minMig'maq / Basques - From one land to another19 h 30 min(GMT-05:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsThe Centre des musiciens du monde presents an unusual encounter between the musical culture of the Basque Country and that of the indigenous Mig’maq nation. The fruit of a creative    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The Centre des musiciens du monde presents an unusual encounter between the musical culture of the Basque Country and that of the indigenous Mig’maq nation. The fruit of a creative residency bringing together artists from these two worlds (Darlène Gijuminag, Claudine Arhancet and Michel Etxekopar), this meeting defies borders and brings together cultures that are brothers by land.\nRevealing both their age-old traditions and the modernity that emanates from their recent collaborations, this concert will be punctuated by the encounter of traditional Mig’maq and Basque music, echoing the traces and faded images of their first encounters. The artists explore both real and imaginary territories, reminding us that the two communities crossed paths centuries ago.\nThis concert is presented in co-production with the SMCQ as part of the Montreal/New Music Festival with the participation of the Basques du Québec Euskaldunak association.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41930_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventCancelled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Kiya Tabassian - Setar from Iran\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/kiya-tabassian-setar-from-iran/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-3-5T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-3-5T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/kiya-600.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>⚠️ATTENTION: CONCERT CANCELLED</strong><br /> <strong>We are sorry to learn that the intimate concert offered by Kiya Tabassian on Wednesday, 5 March 202,5 will not take place for personal reasons. We thank you for your understanding and will keep you informed as soon as possible should a new date be announced.</strong></p> <p>Kiya Tabassian is an Iranian musician recognized for his mastery of the <b>setar</b>, a long-necked Persian lute.</p> <p>His virtuoso technique and innovative approach reinvent the setar. Kiya draws from the richness of Persian poetry and spirituality to infuse emotional depth into his compositions and improvisations.</p> <p>His work is distinguished by a capacity to weave musical stories that transcend cultural boundaries, creating dialogues between the East and the West. As a composer, he also explores new sounds to expand the possibilities of the setar.</p> <p>A leading figure in contemporary Persian music, Kiya Tabassian embodies the union of heritage and innovation.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed05mar20 h 00 minKiya Tabassian - Setar from IranConcert intime20 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event Details⚠️ATTENTION: CONCERT CANCELLED\nWe are sorry to learn that the intimate concert offered by Kiya Tabassian on Wednesday, 5 March 202,5 will not take place for personal reasons. We thank    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                ⚠️ATTENTION: CONCERT CANCELLED\nWe are sorry to learn that the intimate concert offered by Kiya Tabassian on Wednesday, 5 March 202,5 will not take place for personal reasons. We thank you for your understanding and will keep you informed as soon as possible should a new date be announced.\nKiya Tabassian is an Iranian musician recognized for his mastery of the setar, a long-necked Persian lute.\nHis virtuoso technique and innovative approach reinvent the setar. Kiya draws from the richness of Persian poetry and spirituality to infuse emotional depth into his compositions and improvisations.\nHis work is distinguished by a capacity to weave musical stories that transcend cultural boundaries, creating dialogues between the East and the West. As a composer, he also explores new sounds to expand the possibilities of the setar.\nA leading figure in contemporary Persian music, Kiya Tabassian embodies the union of heritage and innovation.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Joseph Church10050, boulevard Gouin Est Montréal (Québec) H1C 1A8{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42283_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-18/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-3-13T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-3-13T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.</p> <p>Inspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.</p> <p>The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.</p> <p>Voices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi<br /> Voice and violin: Janelle Lucyk<br /> Lute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey<br /> Gheychak: Reza Abaee</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Joseph Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"10050, boulevard Gouin Est Montréal (Québec) H1C 1A8\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu13mar19 h 30 minConstellation de cordes19 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Joseph Church\n    Event DetailsThis concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This concert brings together four artists from different musical traditions. You will listen to a combination of traditional Maritime tunes with Rwandan melodies, accompanied by instrumental Baroque melodies on the lute and gheychak.\nInspired by 17th-century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound, constantly transformed by artist Deo Munyakazi’s improvisations on the inanga.\nThe result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak. He adds a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies of traditional Maritime singer Janelle Lucyk.\nVoices and inanga: Deo Munyakazi\nVoice and violin: Janelle Lucyk\nLute and theorbo: Kerry Bursey\nGheychak: Reza Abaee\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Joseph Church10050, boulevard Gouin Est Montréal (Québec) H1C 1A8Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41940_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"!! SOLD OUT !! Nazih Borish - Oud from the Middle East\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/nazih-borish-oud-from-the-middle-east/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-4-16T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-4-16T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Nazih_Borish_14032020_113-photo©Michael-Slobodian-copie-scaled-e1727538622802.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Nazih Borish is a virtuoso of the <b>oud</b>, the Arab string instrument that is the precursor of European lutes, and a renowned musician in the world of oriental music. Born in Syria, he was trained from a young age in the rich Arab musical tradition.</p> <p>His exceptional technique and unique interpretation of the oud have earned him international recognition. He blends tradition and innovation while respecting the essence of classical Arab music. His captivating performances combine subtle improvisations and refined compositions.</p> <p>Nazih Borish is also an accomplished composer, creating works that explore new dimensions of the oud while staying true to its roots.<br /> Through his expressive playing and mastery of the classical Arab repertoire, he is one of the most influential ambassadors of contemporary Arab music, connecting it with other musical traditions worldwide.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed16apr20 h 00 min!! SOLD OUT !! Nazih Borish - Oud from the Middle EastConcert intime20 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsNazih Borish is a virtuoso of the oud, the Arab string instrument that is the precursor of European lutes, and a renowned musician in the world of oriental music. Born in    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Nazih Borish is a virtuoso of the oud, the Arab string instrument that is the precursor of European lutes, and a renowned musician in the world of oriental music. Born in Syria, he was trained from a young age in the rich Arab musical tradition.\nHis exceptional technique and unique interpretation of the oud have earned him international recognition. He blends tradition and innovation while respecting the essence of classical Arab music. His captivating performances combine subtle improvisations and refined compositions.\nNazih Borish is also an accomplished composer, creating works that explore new dimensions of the oud while staying true to its roots.\nThrough his expressive playing and mastery of the classical Arab repertoire, he is one of the most influential ambassadors of contemporary Arab music, connecting it with other musical traditions worldwide.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42866_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Ganbold/Curtet - Diphonic songs from Mongolia\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/ganbold-curtet-diphonic-songs-from-mongolia/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-4-24T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-4-24T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/concert-intime-13.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Immerse yourself in the vast Mongolian steppes with Nasanjargal Ganbold and Johanni Curtet.</p> <p>In Mongolia, traditional music is deeply rooted in the natural environment and the nomadic way of life. At the heart of this sound ecology, Mongols engage in a dialogue with nature through their instruments and voices, blending praises with the art of throat singing.</p> <p>Born in the Altai Mountains, the cradle of khöömii in western Mongolia, Nasanjargal Ganbold is a virtuoso of this unique vocal tradition. He also mastered traditional instruments such as the morin khuur (horsehead fiddle) and the tovshuur (lute). Alongside him, Johanni Curtet, a French ethnomusicologist and throat-singing specialist, brings depth to this musical journey.</p> <p>Their collaboration gives rise to a concert where natural sounds, contemporary poetry, and improvisation intertwine, offering a profound immersion into the soul of Mongolian culture.</p> <p>Recognized as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity by UNESCO in 2010, khöömii embodies the very essence of Mongolian musical tradition.</p> <p><strong>Artists </strong></p> <p><strong>Nasanjargal Ganbold</strong>: khöömii, throat-singing, morin khuur fiddle, tovshuur lute, bishguur (oboe), mouth harp</p> <p><strong>Johanni Curtet</strong>: khöömii, throat-singing, dombra lute, guitar, mouth harp Presented by the Centre des musiciens du monde and Traquen’Art</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu24apr20 h 00 minGanbold/Curtet - Diphonic songs from MongoliaConcert intime20 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsImmerse yourself in the vast Mongolian steppes with Nasanjargal Ganbold and Johanni Curtet.\nIn Mongolia, traditional music is deeply rooted in the natural environment and the nomadic way of life. At    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Immerse yourself in the vast Mongolian steppes with Nasanjargal Ganbold and Johanni Curtet.\nIn Mongolia, traditional music is deeply rooted in the natural environment and the nomadic way of life. At the heart of this sound ecology, Mongols engage in a dialogue with nature through their instruments and voices, blending praises with the art of throat singing.\nBorn in the Altai Mountains, the cradle of khöömii in western Mongolia, Nasanjargal Ganbold is a virtuoso of this unique vocal tradition. He also mastered traditional instruments such as the morin khuur (horsehead fiddle) and the tovshuur (lute). Alongside him, Johanni Curtet, a French ethnomusicologist and throat-singing specialist, brings depth to this musical journey.\nTheir collaboration gives rise to a concert where natural sounds, contemporary poetry, and improvisation intertwine, offering a profound immersion into the soul of Mongolian culture.\nRecognized as Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity by UNESCO in 2010, khöömii embodies the very essence of Mongolian musical tradition.\nArtists \nNasanjargal Ganbold: khöömii, throat-singing, morin khuur fiddle, tovshuur lute, bishguur (oboe), mouth harp\nJohanni Curtet: khöömii, throat-singing, dombra lute, guitar, mouth harp Presented by the Centre des musiciens du monde and Traquen’Art\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tStewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire176 Chem. du Bord-du-Lac-Lakeshore, Pointe-Claire, QC H9S 4J7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42342_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Carnets de soie: echoes from east to west\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/carnets-de-soie-echoes-from-east-to-west-3/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-4-27T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-4-27T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-14-2-scaled-e1726260009258.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, xun) cross the Silk Road from east to west. Their journey invites the audience to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, weaving links between different historical periods as they present music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC &#8211; 9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.</p> <p><strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor)</p> <p><strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng)</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Stewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"176 Chem. du Bord-du-Lac-Lakeshore, Pointe-Claire, QC H9S 4J7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun27apr15 h 00 minCarnets de soie: echoes from east to west15 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Stewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire\n    Event DetailsIn their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, xun) cross the Silk Road from east to west. Their journey invites the audience to follow    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, xun) cross the Silk Road from east to west. Their journey invites the audience to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, weaving links between different historical periods as they present music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC – 9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.\nAnnette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor)\nRan Wang (guzheng)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationStewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire176 Chem. du Bord-du-Lac-Lakeshore, Pointe-Claire, QC H9S 4J7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42592_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Sava - Musique vocale de Croatie (klapa)\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/sava-croatian-polyphonies-klapa/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-5-14T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-5-14T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/concert-intime-2.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Klapa (or klapsko pjevanje) is a multi-part singing tradition from the southern Croatian regions of Dalmatia. Sung in several voices, homophonic and a capella, the term klapa means ‘group of people’. With its rich blend of harmonies, klapa songs celebrate love, wine, homeland and the sea. Since 2012, this traditionally male genre has been included on UNESCO&#8217;s Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity.</p> <p>Sava is a female vocal ensemble performing polyphonic a cappella music from the Balkans. With Sarah Albu, Antonia Branković, Dina Cindrić and Sara Rousseau.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed14may20 h 00 minSava - Musique vocale de Croatie (klapa)Concert intime20 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsKlapa (or klapsko pjevanje) is a multi-part singing tradition from the southern Croatian regions of Dalmatia. Sung in several voices, homophonic and a capella, the term klapa means ‘group of    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Klapa (or klapsko pjevanje) is a multi-part singing tradition from the southern Croatian regions of Dalmatia. Sung in several voices, homophonic and a capella, the term klapa means ‘group of people’. With its rich blend of harmonies, klapa songs celebrate love, wine, homeland and the sea. Since 2012, this traditionally male genre has been included on UNESCO’s Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity.\nSava is a female vocal ensemble performing polyphonic a cappella music from the Balkans. With Sarah Albu, Antonia Branković, Dina Cindrić and Sara Rousseau.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43594_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Bal du Printemps, avec Danse Cadence\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/bal-du-printemps-avec-danse-cadence-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-5-18T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-5-18T17:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Bal-Printemps-2025-1080-3.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Notre <strong>Bal du printemps</strong> annuel aura lieu le <b>dimanche 18 mai, de 14h à 17h</b>, au Centre des musiciens du Monde.</p> <p><b>Danses de la Renaissance, contredanses du 17e au 19e siècle</b> et danse du Mai seront au programme. Les artistes invités.es présenteront également une <b>douzaine de danses</b>, avec des formes plus sophistiquées du répertoire de l&#8217;époque. Ce bal est ouvert à toutes et tous, novices ou expérimenté.es, que vous ayez ou non suivi nos cours.</p> <p><b>À la musique </b>: Annette Bauer aux flûtes, Alexis Chartrand au violon et Margaret Little à la viole de gambe.</p> <p><b>Prestations dansées</b> : avec Anne-Marie Gardette, Pierre Chartrand, Rosalie Chartrand et Shô Araki.</p> <p><b>Maîtres de danse</b> : Anne-Marie Gardette et Pierre Chartrand</p> <p><b>Lieu</b> : Centre des musiciens du monde, 5043, rue Saint-Dominique, Montréal (Québec) H2T 1V1 <b>(accès via l&#8217;église Saint-Enfant-Jésus du Mile-End)</b></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun18may14 h 00 min17 h 00 minBal du Printemps, avec Danse Cadence14 h 00 min - 17 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsNotre Bal du printemps annuel aura lieu le dimanche 18 mai, de 14h à 17h, au Centre des musiciens du Monde.\nDanses de la Renaissance, contredanses du 17e au 19e siècle et danse du Mai    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Notre Bal du printemps annuel aura lieu le dimanche 18 mai, de 14h à 17h, au Centre des musiciens du Monde.\nDanses de la Renaissance, contredanses du 17e au 19e siècle et danse du Mai seront au programme. Les artistes invités.es présenteront également une douzaine de danses, avec des formes plus sophistiquées du répertoire de l’époque. Ce bal est ouvert à toutes et tous, novices ou expérimenté.es, que vous ayez ou non suivi nos cours.\nÀ la musique : Annette Bauer aux flûtes, Alexis Chartrand au violon et Margaret Little à la viole de gambe.\nPrestations dansées : avec Anne-Marie Gardette, Pierre Chartrand, Rosalie Chartrand et Shô Araki.\nMaîtres de danse : Anne-Marie Gardette et Pierre Chartrand\nLieu : Centre des musiciens du monde, 5043, rue Saint-Dominique, Montréal (Québec) H2T 1V1 (accès via l’église Saint-Enfant-Jésus du Mile-End)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tStewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire176 Chem. du Bord-du-Lac-Lakeshore, Pointe-Claire, QC H9S 4J7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_42349_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-20/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-5-18T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-5-18T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Come listen to traditional Rwandan songs and well-known Maritime artists at the String Constellation concert. Inspired by 17<sup>th</sup> century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound. The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak adding a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies from the traditional Maritime repertoire.</p> <p><strong>Deo Munyakszi, </strong>vocals<strong>, </strong>inanga<strong>; Janelle Lucyk, </strong>vocals, violin<strong>; Kerry Bursey, </strong>lute, theorbo<strong>; Reza Abaee, </strong>gheychak</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Stewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"176 Chem. du Bord-du-Lac-Lakeshore, Pointe-Claire, QC H9S 4J7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun18may15 h 00 minConstellation de cordesCAM en tournée15 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Stewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire\n    Event DetailsCome listen to traditional Rwandan songs and well-known Maritime artists at the String Constellation concert. Inspired by 17th century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound. The    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Come listen to traditional Rwandan songs and well-known Maritime artists at the String Constellation concert. Inspired by 17th century musical traditions, voices and instruments create an original tapestry of sound. The result is an astonishing constellation of unique pieces, with Kerry Bursey’s lute and Reza Abaee’s gheychak adding a Baroque and Persian dimension to the Scottish and Irish melodies from the traditional Maritime repertoire.\nDeo Munyakszi, vocals, inanga; Janelle Lucyk, vocals, violin; Kerry Bursey, lute, theorbo; Reza Abaee, gheychak\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationStewart Hall Cultural Centre at Pointe-Claire176 Chem. du Bord-du-Lac-Lakeshore, Pointe-Claire, QC H9S 4J7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43860_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masterclass du grand maître de la musique turque, Fikret Karakaya\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masterclass-du-grand-maitre-de-la-musique-turque-fikret-karakaya-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-5-24T10:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-5-24T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Capture-decran-le-2025-05-09-a-11.45.16.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Fikret Karakaya will be giving a masterclass on 24 and 25 May, from 10 am to 3 pm. It will take place at the Centre des Musiciens du Monde. The aim will be to work on musicality, phrasing, intonation, understanding makams and so on.</p> <p>Here&#8217;s how the masterclasses will work:</p> <p>You bring your instrument and two or three pieces from the Ottoman/Turkish repertoire, with the scores. You will play them in front of Mr Karakaya, and he will advise you on ways of interpreting, on lʼintonation, phrasing, etc.</p> <p>Places are limited, and I would ask you to book your place as soon as possible, before it is full, as well as paying the money for this masterclass. To do this, write to royerartusonicolas@gmail.com.</p> <p>Price of the masterclass: $200 for the two days</p> <p>You can also attend the masterclass as a listener for $50 for both days.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat24may10 h 00 min15 h 00 minMasterclass du grand maître de la musique turque, Fikret Karakaya10 h 00 min - 15 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsFikret Karakaya will be giving a masterclass on 24 and 25 May, from 10 am to 3 pm. It will take place at the Centre des Musiciens du Monde. The    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Fikret Karakaya will be giving a masterclass on 24 and 25 May, from 10 am to 3 pm. It will take place at the Centre des Musiciens du Monde. The aim will be to work on musicality, phrasing, intonation, understanding makams and so on.\nHere’s how the masterclasses will work:\nYou bring your instrument and two or three pieces from the Ottoman/Turkish repertoire, with the scores. You will play them in front of Mr Karakaya, and he will advise you on ways of interpreting, on lʼintonation, phrasing, etc.\nPlaces are limited, and I would ask you to book your place as soon as possible, before it is full, as well as paying the money for this masterclass. To do this, write to royerartusonicolas@gmail.com.\nPrice of the masterclass: $200 for the two days\nYou can also attend the masterclass as a listener for $50 for both days.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43860_1\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masterclass du grand maître de la musique turque, Fikret Karakaya\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masterclass-du-grand-maitre-de-la-musique-turque-fikret-karakaya-2/var/ri-1.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-5-25T10:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-5-25T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Capture-decran-le-2025-05-09-a-11.45.16.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Fikret Karakaya will be giving a masterclass on 24 and 25 May, from 10 am to 3 pm. It will take place at the Centre des Musiciens du Monde. The aim will be to work on musicality, phrasing, intonation, understanding makams and so on.</p> <p>Here&#8217;s how the masterclasses will work:</p> <p>You bring your instrument and two or three pieces from the Ottoman/Turkish repertoire, with the scores. You will play them in front of Mr Karakaya, and he will advise you on ways of interpreting, on lʼintonation, phrasing, etc.</p> <p>Places are limited, and I would ask you to book your place as soon as possible, before it is full, as well as paying the money for this masterclass. To do this, write to royerartusonicolas@gmail.com.</p> <p>Price of the masterclass: $200 for the two days</p> <p>You can also attend the masterclass as a listener for $50 for both days.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun25may10 h 00 min15 h 00 minMasterclass du grand maître de la musique turque, Fikret Karakaya10 h 00 min - 15 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsFikret Karakaya will be giving a masterclass on 24 and 25 May, from 10 am to 3 pm. It will take place at the Centre des Musiciens du Monde. The    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Fikret Karakaya will be giving a masterclass on 24 and 25 May, from 10 am to 3 pm. It will take place at the Centre des Musiciens du Monde. The aim will be to work on musicality, phrasing, intonation, understanding makams and so on.\nHere’s how the masterclasses will work:\nYou bring your instrument and two or three pieces from the Ottoman/Turkish repertoire, with the scores. You will play them in front of Mr Karakaya, and he will advise you on ways of interpreting, on lʼintonation, phrasing, etc.\nPlaces are limited, and I would ask you to book your place as soon as possible, before it is full, as well as paying the money for this masterclass. To do this, write to royerartusonicolas@gmail.com.\nPrice of the masterclass: $200 for the two days\nYou can also attend the masterclass as a listener for $50 for both days.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43782_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Ottoman music with Fikret Karakaya\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/musiques-ottomanes-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-5T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-5T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Capture-decran-le-2025-05-09-a-11.45.16.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Accompanied on the oud/ud by Nicolas Royer-Artuso, the master Fikret Karakaya will demonstrate the richness of Ottoman melodies and the modes specific to this music, as well as the art of ornamentation, through his playing of the kemençe, a small lyre with a powerful sound. This exceptional concert will be a tribute to the great composers of the Ottoman era and to the art of improvisation (taksim).</p> <p>Firket Karakaya is a singer, kemençe and çeng player, composer, musicologist, writer and instrument maker. Until his retirement, he was a musician and presenter for TRT (Turkey&#8217;s national radio station). He is the founder and director of the Bezmara Ensemble, which has been invited to perform in many countries, and has eleven albums to its credit.<br /> Nicolas Royer-Artuso is a composer, musician (oud, electronic violin and fretless guitar), linguist, musicologist and writer. His work has been presented in Germany, England, Armenia, Austria, Brazil, Canada, Colombia, Finland, France, Georgia, Holland, Italy, Lebanon, Lithuania, Poland, Turkey and the United States.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu05jun18 h 00 min19 h 00 minOttoman music with Fikret KarakayaConcerts sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsAccompanied on the oud/ud by Nicolas Royer-Artuso, the master Fikret Karakaya will demonstrate the richness of Ottoman melodies and the modes specific to this music, as well as the art    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Accompanied on the oud/ud by Nicolas Royer-Artuso, the master Fikret Karakaya will demonstrate the richness of Ottoman melodies and the modes specific to this music, as well as the art of ornamentation, through his playing of the kemençe, a small lyre with a powerful sound. This exceptional concert will be a tribute to the great composers of the Ottoman era and to the art of improvisation (taksim).\nFirket Karakaya is a singer, kemençe and çeng player, composer, musicologist, writer and instrument maker. Until his retirement, he was a musician and presenter for TRT (Turkey’s national radio station). He is the founder and director of the Bezmara Ensemble, which has been invited to perform in many countries, and has eleven albums to its credit.\nNicolas Royer-Artuso is a composer, musician (oud, electronic violin and fretless guitar), linguist, musicologist and writer. His work has been presented in Germany, England, Armenia, Austria, Brazil, Canada, Colombia, Finland, France, Georgia, Holland, Italy, Lebanon, Lithuania, Poland, Turkey and the United States.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43641_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"STUDENTS CONCERT\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/students-concert/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-7T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-7T15:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CONCERT-1-920-x-1-080-px-1.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Students concert &#8211; 7 June at 2 p.m.<br /> 📍 Location: Parc Lahaie: 4921, boulevard Saint-Laurent<br /> Montréal (Québec)<br /> (If the weather does not permit, the concert will take place at the Centre des musiciens du monde, 5043 rue Saint-Dominique, just across the street)</p> <p>Programme:<br /> Coming soon</p> <p>Come one, come all to enjoy this wonderful musical afternoon! 🌞🎵</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat07jun14 h 00 min15 h 30 minSTUDENTS CONCERTSpécial ensemble de musique14 h 00 min - 15 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsStudents concert – 7 June at 2 p.m.\n📍 Location: Parc Lahaie: 4921, boulevard Saint-Laurent\nMontréal (Québec)\n(If the weather does not permit, the concert will take place at the    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Students concert – 7 June at 2 p.m.\n📍 Location: Parc Lahaie: 4921, boulevard Saint-Laurent\nMontréal (Québec)\n(If the weather does not permit, the concert will take place at the Centre des musiciens du monde, 5043 rue Saint-Dominique, just across the street)\nProgramme:\nComing soon\nCome one, come all to enjoy this wonderful musical afternoon! 🌞🎵\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeFacebook Event\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43786_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Brazil - Voice of the body\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/lu-horta-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-10T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-10T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/concert-sous-un-arbre-1080-x-1080-px-16.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Voice of the body<br /> A musical experience in which the body becomes a veritable instrument of Brazilian music. With songs, rhythms and movement, this musical experience takes you on a sensitive journey through the living sounds of the body and the voice.<br /> With :<br /> Lu Horta: voice and body percussion<br /> Marcelo Effori: percussion and sampler<br /> Gabriel Shwartz: guitar</p> <p>Lu Horta is a Brazilian artist (singer, composer, body percussionist and teacher). She has a degree in popular music from the Public University of Campinas (UNICAMP). A founding member of the Barbatuques body percussion group, she has helped to create five albums and collaborated on soundtracks (Tropa de Elite, Trash &#8211; City of Hope, Rio 2 and The Boy and the World, nominated for an Oscar in 2016). Lu Horta also has a prolific solo career, with critically acclaimed albums such as Paraíso Eu in 2009 and A Noiva da Cidade in 2013. A committed artist, she uses her voice for social causes, notably in a campaign against violence against women. Since 2023, she has lived in Montreal, where she is involved in artistic collaborations with local artists and educational projects with Orff Québec, UQAM, the Maison des arts participatifs and the Centre des musiciens du monde.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\ttue10jun18 h 00 min19 h 00 minBrazil - Voice of the bodyConcerts sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsVoice of the body\nA musical experience in which the body becomes a veritable instrument of Brazilian music. With songs, rhythms and movement, this musical experience takes you on a    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Voice of the body\nA musical experience in which the body becomes a veritable instrument of Brazilian music. With songs, rhythms and movement, this musical experience takes you on a sensitive journey through the living sounds of the body and the voice.\nWith :\nLu Horta: voice and body percussion\nMarcelo Effori: percussion and sampler\nGabriel Shwartz: guitar\nLu Horta is a Brazilian artist (singer, composer, body percussionist and teacher). She has a degree in popular music from the Public University of Campinas (UNICAMP). A founding member of the Barbatuques body percussion group, she has helped to create five albums and collaborated on soundtracks (Tropa de Elite, Trash – City of Hope, Rio 2 and The Boy and the World, nominated for an Oscar in 2016). Lu Horta also has a prolific solo career, with critically acclaimed albums such as Paraíso Eu in 2009 and A Noiva da Cidade in 2013. A committed artist, she uses her voice for social causes, notably in a campaign against violence against women. Since 2023, she has lived in Montreal, where she is involved in artistic collaborations with local artists and educational projects with Orff Québec, UQAM, the Maison des arts participatifs and the Centre des musiciens du monde.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43790_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Klezmer - between laughter and tears\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/musique-klezmer-en-duo-4/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-17T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-17T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/DSC_4090-copy-scaled.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The klezmer tradition and its danceable yet poignant melodies will be interpreted on clarinet and accordion, two idiomatic instruments of this music that has travelled from Eastern Europe.</p> <p>Gabriel Paquin-Buki is a clarinettist renowned on the Montreal scene for the subtlety of his playing and the diversity of his interpretations. He is a graduate of the Université de Montréal, where he completed a bachelor&#8217;s degree in performance in the class of Jean-François Normand.</p> <p>In 2010, he founded the group Oktopus, an octet of Eastern European music (klezmer, Balkan, classical) with whom he has performed over 250 concerts in Quebec, Canada and Europe. His arrangements and compositions on the albums Lever l&#8217;encre and Hapax have earned him Juno and Canadian Folk Music Award nominations.</p> <p>In 2017, he immersed himself in books to complete a master&#8217;s degree in comparative literature at the Université de Montréal. In his thesis, he explored the delicate subject of laughter in Holocaust literature. Since then, he has divided his time between travelling, music and words.</p> <p>Josh Dolgin, aka Socalled, is a Canadian musician, rapper and producer renowned internationally for his unique style, which blends hip-hop, klezmer, folk music and electro. Born in Montreal, he is also a pianist and accordionist, and has taught the instrument at London&#8217;s Klezfest, where he has also run ‘hiphopkele’ workshops.</p> <p>A key figure on the contemporary klezmer scene, Josh Dolgin has collaborated with renowned artists such as David Krakauer, Michael Winograd, Fred Wesley, Chilly Gonzales, Sophie Solomon and The Mighty Sparrow. His SoCalled collective project has made its mark with concerts such as Hip Hop Hanukkah, which celebrates the meeting of Jewish cultures and urban music.</p> <p>In 2010, the National Film Board of Canada devoted a documentary to him, The ‘Socalled’ Movie, which retraces the adventure of the first ‘Klezmer Cruise’ on the Dnieper River in Ukraine. In 2013, he also wrote the remix of Moe Koffman&#8217;s Curried Soul, which became the official theme for CBC Radio One&#8217;s As It Happens.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\ttue17jun18 h 00 min19 h 00 minKlezmer - between laughter and tearsConcerts sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsThe klezmer tradition and its danceable yet poignant melodies will be interpreted on clarinet and accordion, two idiomatic instruments of this music that has travelled from Eastern Europe.\nGabriel Paquin-Buki is    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The klezmer tradition and its danceable yet poignant melodies will be interpreted on clarinet and accordion, two idiomatic instruments of this music that has travelled from Eastern Europe.\nGabriel Paquin-Buki is a clarinettist renowned on the Montreal scene for the subtlety of his playing and the diversity of his interpretations. He is a graduate of the Université de Montréal, where he completed a bachelor’s degree in performance in the class of Jean-François Normand.\nIn 2010, he founded the group Oktopus, an octet of Eastern European music (klezmer, Balkan, classical) with whom he has performed over 250 concerts in Quebec, Canada and Europe. His arrangements and compositions on the albums Lever l’encre and Hapax have earned him Juno and Canadian Folk Music Award nominations.\nIn 2017, he immersed himself in books to complete a master’s degree in comparative literature at the Université de Montréal. In his thesis, he explored the delicate subject of laughter in Holocaust literature. Since then, he has divided his time between travelling, music and words.\nJosh Dolgin, aka Socalled, is a Canadian musician, rapper and producer renowned internationally for his unique style, which blends hip-hop, klezmer, folk music and electro. Born in Montreal, he is also a pianist and accordionist, and has taught the instrument at London’s Klezfest, where he has also run ‘hiphopkele’ workshops.\nA key figure on the contemporary klezmer scene, Josh Dolgin has collaborated with renowned artists such as David Krakauer, Michael Winograd, Fred Wesley, Chilly Gonzales, Sophie Solomon and The Mighty Sparrow. His SoCalled collective project has made its mark with concerts such as Hip Hop Hanukkah, which celebrates the meeting of Jewish cultures and urban music.\nIn 2010, the National Film Board of Canada devoted a documentary to him, The ‘Socalled’ Movie, which retraces the adventure of the first ‘Klezmer Cruise’ on the Dnieper River in Ukraine. In 2013, he also wrote the remix of Moe Koffman’s Curried Soul, which became the official theme for CBC Radio One’s As It Happens.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_41948_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Federico Tarazona - Charango from Peru\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/federico-tarazona-charango-from-peru/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-18T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-18T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/federico_tarazona.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Federico Tarazona is a Peruvian musician and composer recognized for his virtuosity on the <b>charango</b>, a small traditional guitar from the Andes.</p> <p>His playing skillfully blends traditional Andean rhythms and sounds with contemporary influences. Federico has modernized the charango while preserving its unique character and deep cultural roots. He uses the instrument to create new sound textures, between improvisation and original compositions.</p> <p>In addition to his career as a performer, he is a strong advocate for indigenous music and the cultural richness of the Andes. His work has been widely praised on the international stage, and he is considered one of the ambassadors of modern Andean music.</p> <p>Federico Tarazona continues to share the beauty and complexity of the charango through concerts and international collaborations. This concert will be a unique opportunity to hear him perform solo.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\twed18jun20 h 00 minFederico Tarazona - Charango from PeruConcert intime20 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsFederico Tarazona is a Peruvian musician and composer recognized for his virtuosity on the charango, a small traditional guitar from the Andes.\nHis playing skillfully blends traditional Andean rhythms and sounds with    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Federico Tarazona is a Peruvian musician and composer recognized for his virtuosity on the charango, a small traditional guitar from the Andes.\nHis playing skillfully blends traditional Andean rhythms and sounds with contemporary influences. Federico has modernized the charango while preserving its unique character and deep cultural roots. He uses the instrument to create new sound textures, between improvisation and original compositions.\nIn addition to his career as a performer, he is a strong advocate for indigenous music and the cultural richness of the Andes. His work has been widely praised on the international stage, and he is considered one of the ambassadors of modern Andean music.\nFederico Tarazona continues to share the beauty and complexity of the charango through concerts and international collaborations. This concert will be a unique opportunity to hear him perform solo.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeReserve your ticket\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43794_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Sitaria - Hindustani music\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/uwe-neumann-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-19T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-19T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/thumbnail_Uwe-Neumann.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Sitaria is a musical project led by sitarist Uwe Neumann, accompanied for this concert by percussionist Subir Dev. Sitaria explores the melodic richness and rhythmic power of the Hindustani (North Indian) tradition. The performances are a skilful blend of composition and improvisation, testifying to the musicians&#8217; profound mastery and close working relationship. The sitar, at the heart of the project, is an emblematic instrument born in the 13th century from the encounter between Indian tradition (Veena, ragas) and Persian influences (Rabab).</p> <p>Uwe Neumann is a renowned sitar musician and an ambassador for Indian classical music. A recipient of the Ravi Shankar Memorial Award, he studied for ten years in India with the master Pandit Indranil Bhattacharya, obtaining a Bachelor of Music and a Master of Music (1997) from Visva Bharati University in Shantiniketan. He has been training with Sri Partha Bose since 2009.</p> <p>Founder of the Ragleela group in 1990, he has played at numerous festivals in India, including the Millennium Concert in Benares in 1999, in front of thousands of spectators and dignitaries such as the Dalai Lama and Narendra Modi. Based in Montreal since 2000, he has given over 400 concerts across North America, Europe and India, at prestigious events such as the Montreal International Jazz Festival, Sunfest, and the Vancouver Folk Festival. In addition to Ragleela, he is involved in various projects: Sitaria (sitar-tablas)</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu19jun18 h 00 min19 h 00 minSitaria - Hindustani musicConcerts sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsSitaria is a musical project led by sitarist Uwe Neumann, accompanied for this concert by percussionist Subir Dev. Sitaria explores the melodic richness and rhythmic power of the Hindustani (North    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Sitaria is a musical project led by sitarist Uwe Neumann, accompanied for this concert by percussionist Subir Dev. Sitaria explores the melodic richness and rhythmic power of the Hindustani (North Indian) tradition. The performances are a skilful blend of composition and improvisation, testifying to the musicians’ profound mastery and close working relationship. The sitar, at the heart of the project, is an emblematic instrument born in the 13th century from the encounter between Indian tradition (Veena, ragas) and Persian influences (Rabab).\nUwe Neumann is a renowned sitar musician and an ambassador for Indian classical music. A recipient of the Ravi Shankar Memorial Award, he studied for ten years in India with the master Pandit Indranil Bhattacharya, obtaining a Bachelor of Music and a Master of Music (1997) from Visva Bharati University in Shantiniketan. He has been training with Sri Partha Bose since 2009.\nFounder of the Ragleela group in 1990, he has played at numerous festivals in India, including the Millennium Concert in Benares in 1999, in front of thousands of spectators and dignitaries such as the Dalai Lama and Narendra Modi. Based in Montreal since 2000, he has given over 400 concerts across North America, Europe and India, at prestigious events such as the Montreal International Jazz Festival, Sunfest, and the Vancouver Folk Festival. In addition to Ragleela, he is involved in various projects: Sitaria (sitar-tablas)\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43801_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Ukrainian a cappella songs\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/polyphonies-dukraine-4/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-26T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-26T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/970c6c9a1359bcbc95b1574913dc64ab.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<div class='ewa-rteLine'> <p>The Murmorosi ensemble draws its inspiration from the Ukrainian tradition of polyphonic singing. Their repertoire includes both traditional songs performed a capella and a variety of original compositions and updated rearrangements of Ukrainian folklore.</p> <p>Murmurosi is a Montreal-based ensemble made up of Natalia Telentso and Eli Camilo, accompanied on occasion by guest musicians and singers, dedicated to the transmission of traditional Ukrainian polyphonic song (a UNESCO World Heritage Site). Their a cappella repertoire pays tribute to the ancestral voices of rural Ukraine, with rich, expressive harmonies. Performing at a number of Canadian festivals, they share old songs from village life, full of emotion and beauty. Their debut album, Bohutyn, explores the meeting of traditional songs and contemporary compositions. For this concert, they will be joined by Kateryna Kovshun for a polyphonic trio and a capella performance.</p> </div> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu26jun18 h 00 min19 h 00 minUkrainian a cappella songsConcerts sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsThe Murmorosi ensemble draws its inspiration from the Ukrainian tradition of polyphonic singing. Their repertoire includes both traditional songs performed a capella and a variety of original compositions and    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                \nThe Murmorosi ensemble draws its inspiration from the Ukrainian tradition of polyphonic singing. Their repertoire includes both traditional songs performed a capella and a variety of original compositions and updated rearrangements of Ukrainian folklore.\nMurmurosi is a Montreal-based ensemble made up of Natalia Telentso and Eli Camilo, accompanied on occasion by guest musicians and singers, dedicated to the transmission of traditional Ukrainian polyphonic song (a UNESCO World Heritage Site). Their a cappella repertoire pays tribute to the ancestral voices of rural Ukraine, with rich, expressive harmonies. Performing at a number of Canadian festivals, they share old songs from village life, full of emotion and beauty. Their debut album, Bohutyn, explores the meeting of traditional songs and contemporary compositions. For this concert, they will be joined by Kateryna Kovshun for a polyphonic trio and a capella performance.\n\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44122_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Perse-Inca Duo\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/perse-inca-duo/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-6-28T11:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-6-28T13:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DuoPerseInca@Peter-Graham-scaled-e1726792384658.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>From improvisation to co-composition, the <strong>Perse-Inca Duo</strong> draws on a variety of traditional rhythms and genres, bringing together Middle Eastern modal textures and Andean pentatonics, as well as Eastern melodies and Western harmonies.</p> <p>With <strong>Federico Tarazona</strong>, <em>composition, charango</em> and <strong>Showan Tavakol</strong>, <em>composition, kamancheh.</em></p> <p>Three 30-minute concerts:<br /> 11 a.m., 12 p.m. and 1 p.m.</p> \"}\n\t\t\t\tsat28jun11 h 00 min13 h 30 minPerse-Inca Duo11 h 00 min - 13 h 30 min(GMT+01:00) Parc des Chutes d’Armagh\n    Event DetailsFrom improvisation to co-composition, the Perse-Inca Duo draws on a variety of traditional rhythms and genres, bringing together Middle Eastern modal textures and Andean pentatonics, as well as Eastern melodies    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                From improvisation to co-composition, the Perse-Inca Duo draws on a variety of traditional rhythms and genres, bringing together Middle Eastern modal textures and Andean pentatonics, as well as Eastern melodies and Western harmonies.\nWith Federico Tarazona, composition, charango and Showan Tavakol, composition, kamancheh.\nThree 30-minute concerts:\n11 a.m., 12 p.m. and 1 p.m.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationParc des Chutes d’ArmaghOther Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43808_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Dènkè Dènkè rhythms from Burkina Faso\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/musiques-peulh-du-burkina-faso-4/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-3T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-3T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/DICKO-FILS_Carre_Bio.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Fulani music from Burkina Faso combines song, n&#8217;goni and rhythm to tell the epic story of Fulani life and culture. The deep melodies of the n&#8217;goni (a plucked string instrument originally from West Africa) evoke the vast plains and stories handed down from generation to generation, while the percussion adds an earthly dimension to this celestial music, inviting us to dance and celebrate.</p> <p>Dicko Fils (Moulaye Dicko) is a musician from Burkina Faso of Fulani origin. A master of the kamale n&#8217;goni, he has made a name for himself with his melodious voice and virtuoso playing, fusing the Fulani and Mandingo traditions. After studying the Koran in Mali, he moved to Abidjan, where he discovered reggae, before founding his group Le Faso Kanou in 1992. His first album, Tounga (2005), marked the start of a prolific career with regular releases until 2016. His song Denke Denke became an anthem in West African clubs. In 2016, he won the Kundé d&#8217;Or, Burkina Faso&#8217;s highest musical award, as well as several other prizes, including Best Modern Traditionally Inspired Song with Wakati. In March 2025, he released his 12th album, La Route, recorded between Burkina Faso and Montreal. This opus blends Afrobeat, Mandingo blues and messages of peace, love and living together.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu03jul18 h 00 min19 h 00 minDènkè Dènkè rhythms from Burkina FasoConcerts sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsFulani music from Burkina Faso combines song, n’goni and rhythm to tell the epic story of Fulani life and culture. The deep melodies of the n’goni (a plucked string instrument    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Fulani music from Burkina Faso combines song, n’goni and rhythm to tell the epic story of Fulani life and culture. The deep melodies of the n’goni (a plucked string instrument originally from West Africa) evoke the vast plains and stories handed down from generation to generation, while the percussion adds an earthly dimension to this celestial music, inviting us to dance and celebrate.\nDicko Fils (Moulaye Dicko) is a musician from Burkina Faso of Fulani origin. A master of the kamale n’goni, he has made a name for himself with his melodious voice and virtuoso playing, fusing the Fulani and Mandingo traditions. After studying the Koran in Mali, he moved to Abidjan, where he discovered reggae, before founding his group Le Faso Kanou in 1992. His first album, Tounga (2005), marked the start of a prolific career with regular releases until 2016. His song Denke Denke became an anthem in West African clubs. In 2016, he won the Kundé d’Or, Burkina Faso’s highest musical award, as well as several other prizes, including Best Modern Traditionally Inspired Song with Wakati. In March 2025, he released his 12th album, La Route, recorded between Burkina Faso and Montreal. This opus blends Afrobeat, Mandingo blues and messages of peace, love and living together.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44130_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Solo\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-solo-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-6T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-6T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Design-sans-titre-13.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>With <strong>Mohamed Masmoudi</strong> on traditional oud, solo.</p> \"}\n\t\t\t\tsun06jul14 h 00 min15 h 00 minMasmoudi Solo14 h 00 min - 15 h 00 min(GMT+01:00) Parc Westmount\n    Event DetailsWith Mohamed Masmoudi on traditional oud, solo.    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                With Mohamed Masmoudi on traditional oud, solo.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationParc WestmountOther Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44135_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Gabriel Evangelista solo\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/gabriel-evangelista-solo-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-6T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-6T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/094A3668-1r-e1726788503699.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>For his solo concert, pianist <strong>Gabriel Evangelista</strong> offers us his compositions and arrangements of pieces from the flamenco, jazz and Afro-Cuban repertoires. His expressive style, sometimes gentle, sometimes lively, will energize any audience.</p> <p>Concert will be offer at tha Public Piano on Laurier Avenue, near Querbes street</p> \"}\n\t\t\t\tsun06jul14 h 00 min15 h 00 minGabriel Evangelista soloPiano public14 h 00 min - 15 h 00 min(GMT+01:00) \n    Event DetailsFor his solo concert, pianist Gabriel Evangelista offers us his compositions and arrangements of pieces from the flamenco, jazz and Afro-Cuban repertoires. His expressive style, sometimes gentle, sometimes lively, will    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                For his solo concert, pianist Gabriel Evangelista offers us his compositions and arrangements of pieces from the flamenco, jazz and Afro-Cuban repertoires. His expressive style, sometimes gentle, sometimes lively, will energize any audience.\nConcert will be offer at tha Public Piano on Laurier Avenue, near Querbes street\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43903_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Folk songs from Anatolia\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/folk-songs-from-anatolia/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-8T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-8T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/concert-sous-un-arbre-1080-x-1080-px-10.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Turkish folk music is a living heritage from the many cultures of Anatolia. Rich in regional diversity, it expresses everyday emotions through songs drawing on personal stories. Passed on by türkü singers and aşıks, it combines oral traditions, improvisation, poetry and instruments such as the saz (lute).</p> <p>Born in Ankara and originally from Malatya in Turkey, Sema Gültekin has been immersed in Turkish folk music since childhood. Trained in baglama and music theory, she developed her stage experience at secondary school, while pursuing an MBA at Istanbul&#8217;s Yeditepe University. She perfected her repertoire at the Erdal Erzincan Music Centre. Since moving to Montreal in 2022, she has been helping to promote Turkish folk music through concerts and workshops, both on the local music scene and within Montreal&#8217;s Turkish community.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\ttue08jul18 h 00 min19 h 00 minFolk songs from Anatolia18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsTurkish folk music is a living heritage from the many cultures of Anatolia. Rich in regional diversity, it expresses everyday emotions through songs drawing on personal stories. Passed on by    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Turkish folk music is a living heritage from the many cultures of Anatolia. Rich in regional diversity, it expresses everyday emotions through songs drawing on personal stories. Passed on by türkü singers and aşıks, it combines oral traditions, improvisation, poetry and instruments such as the saz (lute).\nBorn in Ankara and originally from Malatya in Turkey, Sema Gültekin has been immersed in Turkish folk music since childhood. Trained in baglama and music theory, she developed her stage experience at secondary school, while pursuing an MBA at Istanbul’s Yeditepe University. She perfected her repertoire at the Erdal Erzincan Music Centre. Since moving to Montreal in 2022, she has been helping to promote Turkish folk music through concerts and workshops, both on the local music scene and within Montreal’s Turkish community.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43913_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Georgian polyphonies - Echoes of Sakartvelo\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/georgian-polyphonies-echoes-of-sakartvelo/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-10T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-10T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ori-Shalva.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Georgian polyphony is one of the oldest and most complex of singing traditions. Family singing plays an essential role, having enabled it to survive through centuries of invasions and occupations. For Shalva Makharashvili, Andrea Kuzmich and their sons Shalva-Lucas and Gabo, singing is as natural as breathing, rooted in family celebrations rather than stage performances.</p> <p>Ori Shalva carry on this tradition in Toronto, more than 9,000 km from Georgia. The authenticity of their music stems from years of dedication and a musical heritage handed down from generation to generation.</p> <p>Ori Shalva, also known as the Makharashvili family, is a unique musical ensemble. Formed in Toronto by Shalva Makharashvili and Andrea Kuzmich, both from different cultural and linguistic backgrounds, the group was born out of a shared passion for Georgian polyphony. For over twenty years, together with their children, they have been passing on and keeping alive this complex singing tradition, recognised by UNESCO as part of humanity&#8217;s intangible heritage. Their performances offer audiences a rare opportunity to appreciate a living tradition that is still largely unknown outside the Caucasus.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu10jul18 h 00 min19 h 00 minGeorgian polyphonies - Echoes of Sakartvelomusiques sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsGeorgian polyphony is one of the oldest and most complex of singing traditions. Family singing plays an essential role, having enabled it to survive through centuries of invasions and occupations.    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Georgian polyphony is one of the oldest and most complex of singing traditions. Family singing plays an essential role, having enabled it to survive through centuries of invasions and occupations. For Shalva Makharashvili, Andrea Kuzmich and their sons Shalva-Lucas and Gabo, singing is as natural as breathing, rooted in family celebrations rather than stage performances.\nOri Shalva carry on this tradition in Toronto, more than 9,000 km from Georgia. The authenticity of their music stems from years of dedication and a musical heritage handed down from generation to generation.\nOri Shalva, also known as the Makharashvili family, is a unique musical ensemble. Formed in Toronto by Shalva Makharashvili and Andrea Kuzmich, both from different cultural and linguistic backgrounds, the group was born out of a shared passion for Georgian polyphony. For over twenty years, together with their children, they have been passing on and keeping alive this complex singing tradition, recognised by UNESCO as part of humanity’s intangible heritage. Their performances offer audiences a rare opportunity to appreciate a living tradition that is still largely unknown outside the Caucasus.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43915_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Music from Latin America\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/music-from-latin-america/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-15T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-15T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/CMM_altiplano_jmalobaton-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Discover traditional South American rhythms such as the bambuco, pasillo, Zulian dance and milonga, and the cultural history behind each piece in the Altiplano Ensemble&#8217;s rich repertoire.</p> <p>Altiplano is a young musical ensemble founded in Montreal by three Colombian musicians: Leandro Ruiz, Iván Ortiz and Pedro Botia. Through this project, they are committed to spreading the cultural wealth of their native country by interpreting the traditional rhythms of various Latin American countries.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\ttue15jul18 h 00 min19 h 00 minMusic from Latin Americamusiques sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsDiscover traditional South American rhythms such as the bambuco, pasillo, Zulian dance and milonga, and the cultural history behind each piece in the Altiplano Ensemble’s rich repertoire.\nAltiplano is a young    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Discover traditional South American rhythms such as the bambuco, pasillo, Zulian dance and milonga, and the cultural history behind each piece in the Altiplano Ensemble’s rich repertoire.\nAltiplano is a young musical ensemble founded in Montreal by three Colombian musicians: Leandro Ruiz, Iván Ortiz and Pedro Botia. Through this project, they are committed to spreading the cultural wealth of their native country by interpreting the traditional rhythms of various Latin American countries.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\tLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_43919_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Le Baobab voyageur - a cappella songs from around the world\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/le-baobab-voyageur-a-cappella-songs-from-around-the-world/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-17T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-17T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Photo-Choeur-Baobab-_-Groupe-Mai-2025-3.-1.jpeg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The Chœur Baobab invites you on a journey across the continents, where gospel, African polyphonies, traditional Slavic, South American and indigenous songs all resonate with the same voice.</p> <p>Conducted by Claude Marie Landré, the choir presents a colourful, multilingual repertoire, complete with percussion, choreography and solos. A warm, inclusive and festive performance, true to the spirit of the Baobab voyageur.</p> <p>Chœur Baobab is a Montreal-based vocal ensemble of 23 singers led by conductor Claude Marie Landré, who has been celebrating the richness of a cappella, gospel and world music for over 15 years. Performing songs in their original language, the choir stands out for its lively, expressive performances without scores, combining choreography, percussion and vocal solos. Winner of the 2ᵉ prize at the Concours national pour chœurs amateurs (2019), Baobab has sung at Place des Arts, Festival Nuits d&#8217;Afrique, Igloofest and numerous cultural events in Quebec.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Lahaie Park\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"Montréal, QC H2T 1R7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu17jul18 h 00 min19 h 00 minLe Baobab voyageur - a cappella songs from around the worldmusiques sous un arbre18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT+00:00) Lahaie Park\n    Event DetailsThe Chœur Baobab invites you on a journey across the continents, where gospel, African polyphonies, traditional Slavic, South American and indigenous songs all resonate with the same voice.\nConducted by Claude    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The Chœur Baobab invites you on a journey across the continents, where gospel, African polyphonies, traditional Slavic, South American and indigenous songs all resonate with the same voice.\nConducted by Claude Marie Landré, the choir presents a colourful, multilingual repertoire, complete with percussion, choreography and solos. A warm, inclusive and festive performance, true to the spirit of the Baobab voyageur.\nChœur Baobab is a Montreal-based vocal ensemble of 23 singers led by conductor Claude Marie Landré, who has been celebrating the richness of a cappella, gospel and world music for over 15 years. Performing songs in their original language, the choir stands out for its lively, expressive performances without scores, combining choreography, percussion and vocal solos. Winner of the 2ᵉ prize at the Concours national pour chœurs amateurs (2019), Baobab has sung at Place des Arts, Festival Nuits d’Afrique, Igloofest and numerous cultural events in Quebec.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationLahaie ParkMontréal, QC H2T 1R7Other Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44155_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Siraba outdoor concert\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/siraba-outdoor-concert/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-27T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-27T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/2023_11_27_ADAMA-DAOU16745-copie-scaled-e1727542495185.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><em>Siraba</em> means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents&#8230;<br /> Attend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!</p> <p><strong>Musicians :</strong> <strong>Adama Daou</strong>: balafon;<strong> Gabriel Schwartz</strong>: flute, pandeiro; <strong>Aboulaye Koné</strong>: electric guitar; <strong>Christian Obam</strong>: electric bass</p> <p><strong>Pre-concert workshop:</strong> discovery and introduction to the balafon by Adama Daou, from 3:30 to 4:30 p.m.</p> \"}\n\t\t\t\tsun27jul19 h 00 min20 h 00 minSiraba outdoor concert19 h 00 min - 20 h 00 min(GMT+01:00) Parc de Deauville\n    Event DetailsSiraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians : Adama    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Siraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians : Adama Daou: balafon; Gabriel Schwartz: flute, pandeiro; Aboulaye Koné: electric guitar; Christian Obam: electric bass\nPre-concert workshop: discovery and introduction to the balafon by Adama Daou, from 3:30 to 4:30 p.m.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationParc de DeauvilleOther Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44163_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Siraba Laval\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/siraba-laval-3/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-31T17:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-31T18:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/2023_11_27_ADAMA-DAOU16745-copie-scaled-e1727542495185.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><em>Siraba</em> means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents&#8230;<br /> Attend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!</p> <p><strong>Musicians:</strong> <strong>Adama Daou</strong>: balafon; <strong>Gabriel Schwartz</strong>: flute, pandeiro; <strong>Aboulaye Koné</strong>: electric guitar; <strong>Christian Obam</strong>: electric bass</p> <p>An onstage discussion with the artists will take place after the show.</p> <p>Concert offered as part of Zones musicales at Maison des Arts de Laval.</p> \"}\n\t\t\t\tthu31jul17 h 30 min18 h 30 minSiraba Laval17 h 30 min - 18 h 30 min(GMT+01:00) Maison des Arts de Laval\n    Event DetailsSiraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians: Adama Daou:    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Siraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians: Adama Daou: balafon; Gabriel Schwartz: flute, pandeiro; Aboulaye Koné: electric guitar; Christian Obam: electric bass\nAn onstage discussion with the artists will take place after the show.\nConcert offered as part of Zones musicales at Maison des Arts de Laval.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison des Arts de LavalOther Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44141_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Siraba Laval 2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/siraba-laval-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-7-31T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-7-31T21:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/2023_11_27_ADAMA-DAOU16745-copie-scaled-e1727542495185.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><em>Siraba</em> means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents&#8230;<br /> Attend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!</p> <p><strong>Musicians:</strong> <strong>Adama Daou</strong>: balafon; <strong>Gabriel Schwartz</strong>: flute, pandeiro; <strong>Aboulaye Koné</strong>: electric guitar; <strong>Christian Obam</strong>: electric bass</p> <p>An onstage discussion with the artists will take place after the show.</p> <p>Concert offered as part of Zones musicales at Maison des Arts de Laval.</p> \"}\n\t\t\t\tthu31jul20 h 00 min21 h 00 minSiraba Laval 220 h 00 min - 21 h 00 min(GMT+01:00) Maison des Arts de Laval\n    Event DetailsSiraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians: Adama Daou:    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Siraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians: Adama Daou: balafon; Gabriel Schwartz: flute, pandeiro; Aboulaye Koné: electric guitar; Christian Obam: electric bass\nAn onstage discussion with the artists will take place after the show.\nConcert offered as part of Zones musicales at Maison des Arts de Laval.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison des Arts de LavalOther Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44306_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Constellation de cordes - Virée classique\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/constellation-de-cordes-viree-classique-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-8-17T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-8-17T14:45-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/media-social-festival-2023-1080x1080-1.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Against a backdrop of 17th-century sounds, the voices and instruments of the<strong><em> Constellation de cordes</em></strong> project blend and overlap to weave a work constantly renewed by the improvisations of Deo Munyakazi (Rwanda) on his inanga zither.</p> <p><strong>Artists: Janelle Lucyck</strong>, <em>violin &amp; vocals</em> | <strong>Deo Munyakazi</strong>, <em>inanga &amp; vocals</em> | <strong>Kerry Bursey</strong>, <em>theorbo</em> | <strong>Reza Abaee</strong>, <em>ghaychak fiddle</em></p> <p>Free concert as part of the <strong>Orchestre Symphonique de Montréal&#8217;s Virée Classique OSM</strong>.</p> \"}\n\t\t\t\tsun17aug14 h 00 min14 h 45 minConstellation de cordes - Virée classique14 h 00 min - 14 h 45 min(GMT+01:00) \n    Event DetailsAgainst a backdrop of 17th-century sounds, the voices and instruments of the Constellation de cordes project blend and overlap to weave a work constantly renewed by the improvisations of Deo    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Against a backdrop of 17th-century sounds, the voices and instruments of the Constellation de cordes project blend and overlap to weave a work constantly renewed by the improvisations of Deo Munyakazi (Rwanda) on his inanga zither.\nArtists: Janelle Lucyck, violin & vocals | Deo Munyakazi, inanga & vocals | Kerry Bursey, theorbo | Reza Abaee, ghaychak fiddle\nFree concert as part of the Orchestre Symphonique de Montréal’s Virée Classique OSM.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44517_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Tur Malka (The King&#039;s Mountain) - New Yiddish Songs from Canada\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/tur-malka-the-kings-mountain-new-yiddish-songs-from-canada/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-9-17T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-9-17T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CONCERT-1.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The language of Eastern European Jews, Yiddish made its way to Canada with successive waves of immigration in the 20th century. Between deep roots and contemporary creations, it resonates here in original songs inspired by exile, memory, loss, but also hope, love, humor, and tenderness.</p> <p>The concert<strong><em> Tur Malka (The King&#8217;s Mountain) &#8211; New Yiddish Songs from Canada</em></strong> explores this original <strong>vocal</strong> repertoire in a refined acoustic format, performed by a <strong>quartet</strong> (piano, violin, cello, double bass).</p> <p>An intimate and vibrant concert, with simple and powerful melodies, where the past meets the present in a language that sings delightfully to our ears.</p> <p><strong>Artists :</strong><br /> Viola: Elvira Misbakhova<br /> Double bass, arrangements: Mael Oudin<br /> Cello: Sheila Hannigan<br /> Piano, guitar, accordion, vocals, compositions, arrangements: Henri Oppenheim</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed17sep19 h 30 min20 h 30 minTur Malka (The King's Mountain) - New Yiddish Songs from CanadaConcert intime19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT+01:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsThe language of Eastern European Jews, Yiddish made its way to Canada with successive waves of immigration in the 20th century. Between deep roots and contemporary creations, it resonates here    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The language of Eastern European Jews, Yiddish made its way to Canada with successive waves of immigration in the 20th century. Between deep roots and contemporary creations, it resonates here in original songs inspired by exile, memory, loss, but also hope, love, humor, and tenderness.\nThe concert Tur Malka (The King’s Mountain) – New Yiddish Songs from Canada explores this original vocal repertoire in a refined acoustic format, performed by a quartet (piano, violin, cello, double bass).\nAn intimate and vibrant concert, with simple and powerful melodies, where the past meets the present in a language that sings delightfully to our ears.\nArtists :\nViola: Elvira Misbakhova\nDouble bass, arrangements: Mael Oudin\nCello: Sheila Hannigan\nPiano, guitar, accordion, vocals, compositions, arrangements: Henri Oppenheim\n \n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44678_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Gittern and medieval lute workshop\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/gittern-and-medieval-lute-workshop/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-9-25T12:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-9-25T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Stage-de-guiterneluth-m-1.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><span data-contrast='auto'>This workshop will focus on the playing technique for <strong>gittern</strong> and <strong>medieval lute</strong>, with comparative approach to the plectrum technique of non-european plucked chordophones. </span><span data-ccp-props='{}'> </span></p> <p><span data-contrast='auto'>The seminar is aimed at professionals and amateur medieval music performers and renaissance lute players who want to approach plectrum technique. It will consist of an overview of different technical solutions: plectrum, plectrum and fingers, intabulation and strumming techniques, and a reflection on the role of plucked instruments in various medieval and late-medieval repertoires.</span><span data-ccp-props='{}'> </span></p> <p><em>Peppe Frana biography:</em><span data-ccp-props='{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:0}'><em> </em><br /> </span><span data-contrast='auto'>Passionate about music from an early age, he began with rock guitar before immersing himself in modal traditions inspired by composer and musician Ross Daly. He studied oud and plectrum instruments in Greece and Turkey with masters such as Yurdal Tokcan and Ömer Erdoğdular. A meeting with Ensemble Micrologus sparked his interest in medieval European music, and he soon became a leading specialist in Italian Trecento repertoire. Since 2013, he has studied medieval lute at the </span><i><span data-contrast='auto'>Schola Cantorum Basiliensis</span></i><span data-contrast='auto'> under musicologist and lutenist Crawford Young. He holds a degree in Philosophy and regularly performs at major musical festivals across Italy and internationally.</span><span data-ccp-props='{}'> </span></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu25sep12 h 00 min15 h 00 minGittern and medieval lute workshopStage - Worshop12 h 00 min - 15 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsThis workshop will focus on the playing technique for gittern and medieval lute, with comparative approach to the plectrum technique of non-european plucked chordophones.  \nThe seminar is    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This workshop will focus on the playing technique for gittern and medieval lute, with comparative approach to the plectrum technique of non-european plucked chordophones.  \nThe seminar is aimed at professionals and amateur medieval music performers and renaissance lute players who want to approach plectrum technique. It will consist of an overview of different technical solutions: plectrum, plectrum and fingers, intabulation and strumming techniques, and a reflection on the role of plucked instruments in various medieval and late-medieval repertoires. \nPeppe Frana biography: \nPassionate about music from an early age, he began with rock guitar before immersing himself in modal traditions inspired by composer and musician Ross Daly. He studied oud and plectrum instruments in Greece and Turkey with masters such as Yurdal Tokcan and Ömer Erdoğdular. A meeting with Ensemble Micrologus sparked his interest in medieval European music, and he soon became a leading specialist in Italian Trecento repertoire. Since 2013, he has studied medieval lute at the Schola Cantorum Basiliensis under musicologist and lutenist Crawford Young. He holds a degree in Philosophy and regularly performs at major musical festivals across Italy and internationally. \n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSpadina Theatre - Alliance française de Toronto24 Spadina Rd{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44313_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Carnets de soie - Toronto\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/carnets-de-soie-toronto-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-9-27T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-9-27T21:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-30-scaled-e1726263783551.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Discover an itinerary where each note becomes a pause on the path to discovering the Other. The artists celebrate the richness of their respective cultures (Persian and Mongolian), woven together like silk threads, seeking harmonies beyond borders and distances.</p> <p>With the morin khuur (horse-headed fiddle) and the santur (table zither), melodies intertwine like the paths that crisscross the desert and steppe.</p> <p><strong>Artists: Uuriintuya Khalivan</strong>, m<em>orin-khuur</em> | <strong>Sadaf Amini</strong>, <em>santur</em></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Spadina Theatre - Alliance française de Toronto\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"24 Spadina Rd\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat27sep20 h 00 min21 h 00 minCarnets de soie - Toronto20 h 00 min - 21 h 00 min(GMT+01:00) Spadina Theatre - Alliance française de Toronto\n    Event DetailsDiscover an itinerary where each note becomes a pause on the path to discovering the Other. The artists celebrate the richness of their respective cultures (Persian and Mongolian), woven together    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Discover an itinerary where each note becomes a pause on the path to discovering the Other. The artists celebrate the richness of their respective cultures (Persian and Mongolian), woven together like silk threads, seeking harmonies beyond borders and distances.\nWith the morin khuur (horse-headed fiddle) and the santur (table zither), melodies intertwine like the paths that crisscross the desert and steppe.\nArtists: Uuriintuya Khalivan, morin-khuur | Sadaf Amini, santur\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSpadina Theatre - Alliance française de Toronto24 Spadina RdOther Events\n\t\t\n\t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44320_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Siraba - Centre Sanaaq\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/siraba-centre-sanaaq-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-10-1T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-10-1T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/2023_11_27_ADAMA-DAOU16745-copie-scaled-e1727542495185.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><em>Siraba</em> means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents&#8230;<br /> Attend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!</p> <p><strong>Musicians:</strong> <strong>Adama Daou</strong>: <em>balafon</em>;<strong> Gabriel Schwartz</strong>: <em>flute, pandeiro</em>; <strong>Aboulaye Koné</strong>: <em>electric guitar</em>; <strong>Christian Obam</strong>: <em>electric bass</em></p> \"}\n\t\t\t\twed01oct19 h 30 min20 h 30 minSiraba - Centre Sanaaq19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT+01:00) Centre culturel et communautaire Sanaaq\n    Event DetailsSiraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians: Adama Daou:    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Siraba means the great way, a proposal for dialogue between 3 continents…\nAttend an outdoor concert featuring the ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America and Europe!\nMusicians: Adama Daou: balafon; Gabriel Schwartz: flute, pandeiro; Aboulaye Koné: electric guitar; Christian Obam: electric bass\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre culturel et communautaire SanaaqOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44821_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Los Gemelos : Evangelista &amp; Santos\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/los-gemelos-evangelista-santos-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-10-8T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-10-8T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Capture-decran-2025-09-23-123134.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This nickname, which means “the twins,” evokes their resemblance and complicity: on one side, a Spanish pianist dedicated to Cuban music who also plays percussion, and on the other, a Cuban percussionist dedicated to Spanish music who also plays piano.</p> \",\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture de Rosemont–La Petite-Patrie\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed08oct19 h 30 min20 h 30 minLos Gemelos : Evangelista & SantosConcert HLM19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Maison de la culture de Rosemont–La Petite-Patrie\n    Event DetailsThis nickname, which means “the twins,” evokes their resemblance and complicity: on one side, a Spanish pianist dedicated to Cuban music who also plays percussion, and on the other, a    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This nickname, which means “the twins,” evokes their resemblance and complicity: on one side, a Spanish pianist dedicated to Cuban music who also plays percussion, and on the other, a Cuban percussionist dedicated to Spanish music who also plays piano.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture de Rosemont–La Petite-PatrieOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture Janine-Sutto2550 Rue Ontario Est Montréal, QC H2K 1W7\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44825_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Silk Road diaries Echoes from east to west in Ville-Marie\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/silk-road-diaries-echoes-from-east-to-west-in-ville-marie/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-10-15T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-10-15T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/19_jun_CMM_jmalobaton_-13-e1725711929972.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>In their musical encounter, musicians <strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng) and <strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor) traverse the silk road from East to West. Their journey invites the audience along a geographical route from China via India to Italy. Together, they weave through different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200BC-9AD) to music from the emerging European 15<sup>th</sup> century Renaissance.</p> <p>The program equally imagines and draws inspirations from different physical and emotional landscapes that might be encountered by a timeless traveller – from witnessing a deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to adventurously daring to set out on a long journey, to the loneliness that a traveller can experience far away from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments, and the manifold vibrations of their strings, giving room for improvisations, and an exploration of the unknown.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture Janine-Sutto\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"2550 Rue Ontario Est Montréal, QC H2K 1W7\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture Janine-Sutto\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed15oct19 h 30 min20 h 30 minSilk Road diaries Echoes from east to west in Ville-MarieConcert HLM19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Maison de la culture Janine-Sutto\n    Event DetailsIn their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor) traverse the silk road from East to West. Their journey invites the audience    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor) traverse the silk road from East to West. Their journey invites the audience along a geographical route from China via India to Italy. Together, they weave through different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200BC-9AD) to music from the emerging European 15th century Renaissance.\nThe program equally imagines and draws inspirations from different physical and emotional landscapes that might be encountered by a timeless traveller – from witnessing a deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to adventurously daring to set out on a long journey, to the loneliness that a traveller can experience far away from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments, and the manifold vibrations of their strings, giving room for improvisations, and an exploration of the unknown.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture Janine-Sutto2550 Rue Ontario Est Montréal, QC H2K 1W7Other Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45435_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Silk Diaries - From Persia to Mongolia - Amal&#039;Gamme\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/silk-diaries-from-persia-to-mongolia-amalgamme/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-10-25T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-10-25T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-29-scaled-e1726264210452.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>On the musical paths leading to the Silk Road, <strong>Uuriintuya Khalivan</strong>, carrying the breath of Mongolia, and <strong>Sadaf Amini</strong>, carrying the echoes of Iran, met in Montreal. Together, they chart their own course, where each note becomes a pause on the path to discovering the Other. They celebrate the richness of their respective cultures, woven like silk threads, seeking harmonies beyond borders, beyond distances.</p> <p>With the morin khuur (horsehead fiddle) and the santur (table zither), they create melodies that intertwine like the paths that crisscross the desert and the steppe. Their music resonates like an echo of centuries past, a testament to beauty and diversity, a vibrant tribute to the timeless magic of the Silk Road.</p> \",\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Amal&#039;Gamme\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat25oct19 h 30 min20 h 30 minSilk Diaries - From Persia to Mongolia - Amal'GammeConcert HLM19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Salle de concert Saint-François-Xavier\n    Event DetailsOn the musical paths leading to the Silk Road, Uuriintuya Khalivan, carrying the breath of Mongolia, and Sadaf Amini, carrying the echoes of Iran, met in Montreal. Together, they chart    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                On the musical paths leading to the Silk Road, Uuriintuya Khalivan, carrying the breath of Mongolia, and Sadaf Amini, carrying the echoes of Iran, met in Montreal. Together, they chart their own course, where each note becomes a pause on the path to discovering the Other. They celebrate the richness of their respective cultures, woven like silk threads, seeking harmonies beyond borders, beyond distances.\nWith the morin khuur (horsehead fiddle) and the santur (table zither), they create melodies that intertwine like the paths that crisscross the desert and the steppe. Their music resonates like an echo of centuries past, a testament to beauty and diversity, a vibrant tribute to the timeless magic of the Silk Road.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSalle de concert Saint-François-XavierOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45120_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Silk Road diaries from Persia to Mongolia in Ste-Thérèse city\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/silk-road-diaries-from-persia-to-mongolia-in-ste-therese-city/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-10-26T11:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-10-26T12:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-29-scaled-e1726264210452.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Uuriintuya Khalivan (Mongolia) and Sadaf Amini (Iran) met in Montreal, sparking a musical journey at the Silk Roads’ crossroads. Together, they blend their unique musical backgrounds, where each note is a step on a meandering path. The duo celebrates their own respective cultures, woven together like a silk thread, searching for harmonies beyond borders and distances.</p> <p>With the morin-khuur (horsehead fiddle) and santur (hammered dulcimer), they weave melodies, like threads of silk, reminiscent of paths across the desert and the steppes, echoing the timeless magic of the infamous Silk Road.</p> \",\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Maison Lachaîne\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun26oct11 h 00 min12 h 00 minSilk Road diaries from Persia to Mongolia in Ste-Thérèse cityConcert HLM11 h 00 min - 12 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Maison Lachaîne\n    Event DetailsUuriintuya Khalivan (Mongolia) and Sadaf Amini (Iran) met in Montreal, sparking a musical journey at the Silk Roads’ crossroads. Together, they blend their unique musical backgrounds, where each note is    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Uuriintuya Khalivan (Mongolia) and Sadaf Amini (Iran) met in Montreal, sparking a musical journey at the Silk Roads’ crossroads. Together, they blend their unique musical backgrounds, where each note is a step on a meandering path. The duo celebrates their own respective cultures, woven together like a silk thread, searching for harmonies beyond borders and distances.\nWith the morin-khuur (horsehead fiddle) and santur (hammered dulcimer), they weave melodies, like threads of silk, reminiscent of paths across the desert and the steppes, echoing the timeless magic of the infamous Silk Road.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison LachaîneOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre Culturel St-John593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, Canada\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45118_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Silk Road diaries from Persia to Mongolia in Bromont\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/silk-road-diaries-from-persia-to-mongolia-in-bromont/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-11-2T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-11-2T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/FESTCMM_J2_Vend-29-scaled-e1726264210452.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Uuriintuya Khalivan (Mongolia) and Sadaf Amini (Iran) met in Montreal, sparking a musical journey at the Silk Roads’ crossroads. Together, they blend their unique musical backgrounds, where each note is a step on a meandering path. The duo celebrates their own respective cultures, woven together like a silk thread, searching for harmonies beyond borders and distances.</p> <p>With the morin-khuur (horsehead fiddle) and santur (hammered dulcimer), they weave melodies, like threads of silk, reminiscent of paths across the desert and the steppes, echoing the timeless magic of the infamous Silk Road.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre Culturel St-John\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, Canada\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre Culturel St-John\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun02nov15 h 00 min16 h 00 minSilk Road diaries from Persia to Mongolia in BromontConcert HLM15 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre Culturel St-John\n    Event DetailsUuriintuya Khalivan (Mongolia) and Sadaf Amini (Iran) met in Montreal, sparking a musical journey at the Silk Roads’ crossroads. Together, they blend their unique musical backgrounds, where each note is    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Uuriintuya Khalivan (Mongolia) and Sadaf Amini (Iran) met in Montreal, sparking a musical journey at the Silk Roads’ crossroads. Together, they blend their unique musical backgrounds, where each note is a step on a meandering path. The duo celebrates their own respective cultures, woven together like a silk thread, searching for harmonies beyond borders and distances.\nWith the morin-khuur (horsehead fiddle) and santur (hammered dulcimer), they weave melodies, like threads of silk, reminiscent of paths across the desert and the steppes, echoing the timeless magic of the infamous Silk Road.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre Culturel St-John593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, CanadaOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44674_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Introductory workshop to Moroccan chaabi singing\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/introductory-workshop-to-moroccan-chaabi-singing/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-11-7T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-11-7T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Site-Atelier-Chaabi-1.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>Want to sing, travel, and discover vibrant and festive folk music? This workshop is for you!</strong></p> <p>For several years now, singer <strong>Laïla Amezian</strong> has been offering workshops open to everyone, with no prerequisites, to introduce them to Moroccan chaabi singing. Chaabi is the voice of the people: music rooted in everyday life, rhythmic, warm, joyful, but also conveying profound and sometimes politically engaged stories.</p> <p>The workshop is not limited to simple vocal practice: it is a true sensory immersion into the musical world of chaabi through voice and rhythm. You will be invited to feel the music from within, to discover poetic lyrics and the stories they tell, and the emotions they convey.</p> <p>This collective experience is also an opportunity to immerse yourself in a living culture, to understand its codes, symbols, and often overlooked richness. Special attention is paid to the diversity of chaabi styles in the northern part of the country and the essential role of women in this musical tradition.</p> <p>No musical experience is required: all you need is the desire to discover, share, and let your voice resonate with that of the group. At the end of the workshop, you will leave with a few song excerpts and their translations in hand, as well as simple rhythmic cues and elements to extend the experience at home or with others.</p> <p><strong>A warm and accessible workshop, to be enjoyed as a moment of pleasure, exchange, and openness.</strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri07nov18 h 00 min20 h 00 minIntroductory workshop to Moroccan chaabi singingAtelier18 h 00 min - 20 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsWant to sing, travel, and discover vibrant and festive folk music? This workshop is for you!\nFor several years now, singer Laïla Amezian has been offering workshops open to everyone, with    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Want to sing, travel, and discover vibrant and festive folk music? This workshop is for you!\nFor several years now, singer Laïla Amezian has been offering workshops open to everyone, with no prerequisites, to introduce them to Moroccan chaabi singing. Chaabi is the voice of the people: music rooted in everyday life, rhythmic, warm, joyful, but also conveying profound and sometimes politically engaged stories.\nThe workshop is not limited to simple vocal practice: it is a true sensory immersion into the musical world of chaabi through voice and rhythm. You will be invited to feel the music from within, to discover poetic lyrics and the stories they tell, and the emotions they convey.\nThis collective experience is also an opportunity to immerse yourself in a living culture, to understand its codes, symbols, and often overlooked richness. Special attention is paid to the diversity of chaabi styles in the northern part of the country and the essential role of women in this musical tradition.\nNo musical experience is required: all you need is the desire to discover, share, and let your voice resonate with that of the group. At the end of the workshop, you will leave with a few song excerpts and their translations in hand, as well as simple rhythmic cues and elements to extend the experience at home or with others.\nA warm and accessible workshop, to be enjoyed as a moment of pleasure, exchange, and openness.\n \n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture Marie-Uguay6052 Bd Monk, Montréal, QC H4E 3H6\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44830_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Silk Road diaries - Echoes from east to west in Ville-Émard\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/silk-road-diaries-echoes-from-east-to-west-south-east/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-11-8T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-11-8T15:15-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/19_jun_CMM_jmalobaton_-13-e1725711929972.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>In their musical encounter, musicians <strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng) and <strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor) traverse the silk road from East to West. Their journey invites the audience along a geographical route from China via India to Italy. Together, they weave through different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200BC-9AD) to music from the emerging European 15<sup>th</sup> century Renaissance.</p> <p>The program equally imagines and draws inspirations from different physical and emotional landscapes that might be encountered by a timeless traveller – from witnessing a deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to adventurously daring to set out on a long journey, to the loneliness that a traveller can experience far away from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments, and the manifold vibrations of their strings, giving room for improvisations, and an exploration of the unknown.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture Marie-Uguay\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"6052 Bd Monk, Montréal, QC H4E 3H6\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture Marie-Uguay\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat08nov14 h 00 min15 h 15 minSilk Road diaries - Echoes from east to west in Ville-ÉmardConcert HLM14 h 00 min - 15 h 15 min(GMT-05:00) Maison de la culture Marie-Uguay\n    Event DetailsIn their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor) traverse the silk road from East to West. Their journey invites the audience    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor) traverse the silk road from East to West. Their journey invites the audience along a geographical route from China via India to Italy. Together, they weave through different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200BC-9AD) to music from the emerging European 15th century Renaissance.\nThe program equally imagines and draws inspirations from different physical and emotional landscapes that might be encountered by a timeless traveller – from witnessing a deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes, to adventurously daring to set out on a long journey, to the loneliness that a traveller can experience far away from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments, and the manifold vibrations of their strings, giving room for improvisations, and an exploration of the unknown.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture Marie-Uguay6052 Bd Monk, Montréal, QC H4E 3H6Other Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre Culturel St-John593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, Canada\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45441_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Annette Bauer &amp; Ran Wang in Bromont\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/annette-bauer-ran-wang-in-bromont/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-11-9T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-11-9T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/19_jun_CMM_jmalobaton_-13-e1725711929972.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>In their musical encounter, musicians <strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng) and <strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor) travel the Silk Road from east to west. Their journey invites the audience to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, also weaving links between different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC–9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.</p> <p>The program is also inspired by the different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveler might encounter—from observing deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveler might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments and the multiple vibrations of their strings, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre Culturel St-John\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, Canada\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre Culturel St-John\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun09nov15 h 00 min16 h 00 minAnnette Bauer & Ran Wang in BromontConcert HLM15 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre Culturel St-John\n    Event DetailsIn their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor) travel the Silk Road from east to west. Their journey invites the audience to follow    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor) travel the Silk Road from east to west. Their journey invites the audience to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, also weaving links between different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC–9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.\nThe program is also inspired by the different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveler might encounter—from observing deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveler might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments and the multiple vibrations of their strings, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre Culturel St-John593 Shefford street, Bromont, QC, CanadaOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture de Rosemont–La Petite-Patrie6707 Av. De Lorimier, Montréal, QC H2G 1J6\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44814_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Andalusyria in Waterloo\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/andalusyria-in-waterloo/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-11-13T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-11-13T21:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Creation-sans-titre-7-2-e1726793557547.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>Andalusyria</strong> brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arabic traditions.<br /> <strong>Nazih Borish</strong>, a musician based in Montreal, is a self-taught oud virtuoso who founded his own music school in his hometown of Lattakia, Syria. <strong>Gabriel Evangelista</strong>, a Montrealer of Spanish origin, is a flamenco-jazz pianist. Both have developed their own musical language throughout their careers and are committed to this artistic encounter that links their cultural and personal horizons.</p> <p>The result: great poetry built on flights of improvised notes, unique from one performance to the next.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture de Rosemont–La Petite-Patrie\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"6707 Av. De Lorimier, Montréal, QC H2G 1J6\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Maison de la Culture De Waterloo\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu13nov20 h 00 min21 h 00 minAndalusyria in WaterlooConcert HLM20 h 00 min - 21 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Maison de la culture de Rosemont–La Petite-Patrie\n    Event DetailsAndalusyria brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arabic traditions.\nNazih Borish, a musician based in Montreal, is a self-taught    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Andalusyria brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arabic traditions.\nNazih Borish, a musician based in Montreal, is a self-taught oud virtuoso who founded his own music school in his hometown of Lattakia, Syria. Gabriel Evangelista, a Montrealer of Spanish origin, is a flamenco-jazz pianist. Both have developed their own musical language throughout their careers and are committed to this artistic encounter that links their cultural and personal horizons.\nThe result: great poetry built on flights of improvised notes, unique from one performance to the next.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture de Rosemont–La Petite-Patrie6707 Av. De Lorimier, Montréal, QC H2G 1J6Other Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44844_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Kayhan Kalhor &amp; Erdal Erzincan\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/kayhan-kalhor-erdal-erzincan-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-11-22T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-11-22T21:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<div class='tuxCmsEdit__webEventSelection--subtitle'>Master Concert</div> <div class='tuxCmsEdit__webEventSelection--category'>In this rare meeting of musical masters, two of the world&#8217;s foremost exponents of ancient traditions converge to reveal a repertoire of exceptional beauty and depth.</div> <div class='tuxCmsEdit__webEventSelection--description'> <p>Iranian kamancheh virtuoso <strong>Kayhan Kalhor</strong> and Anatolian baglama luminary <strong>Erdal Erzincan</strong> have been performing together for over a decade, first capturing their musical dialogue in the acclaimed 2004 recording <em>The Wind</em>. Since then, they have refined their collaboration into a singular musical language, intricate yet expansive, rooted in tradition yet alive with contemporary vitality.</p> <p>Their interplay embodies an unspoken understanding; an artistry that transcends technique and invites audiences into a realm where music dissolves boundaries and speaks directly to the human spirit.</p> <p>Artists:<br /> Kayhan Kalhor – Kamancheh<br /> Erdal Erzincan – Baglama</p> <p>This event is made possible thanks to the support of our partners, the Canada Council for the Arts, the Conseil des arts et des lettres du Québec, the Conseil des arts de Montréal, and its sponsor Matin Tireh Dast, financial advisor.</p> <p><em>Parking is available behind the Musicians&#8217; Center, with entrance on Bullion Street.</em><br /> <em>Reserve your parking spot with <a href='https://clicknpark.com/get-clicknpark-app'>Clicknpark</a>.</em></p> </div> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat22nov20 h 00 min21 h 00 minKayhan Kalhor & Erdal Erzincangrand concert20 h 00 min - 21 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsMaster Concert\nIn this rare meeting of musical masters, two of the world’s foremost exponents of ancient traditions converge to reveal a repertoire of exceptional beauty and depth.\n\nIranian    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Master Concert\nIn this rare meeting of musical masters, two of the world’s foremost exponents of ancient traditions converge to reveal a repertoire of exceptional beauty and depth.\n\nIranian kamancheh virtuoso Kayhan Kalhor and Anatolian baglama luminary Erdal Erzincan have been performing together for over a decade, first capturing their musical dialogue in the acclaimed 2004 recording The Wind. Since then, they have refined their collaboration into a singular musical language, intricate yet expansive, rooted in tradition yet alive with contemporary vitality.\nTheir interplay embodies an unspoken understanding; an artistry that transcends technique and invites audiences into a realm where music dissolves boundaries and speaks directly to the human spirit.\nArtists:\nKayhan Kalhor – Kamancheh\nErdal Erzincan – Baglama\nThis event is made possible thanks to the support of our partners, the Canada Council for the Arts, the Conseil des arts et des lettres du Québec, the Conseil des arts de Montréal, and its sponsor Matin Tireh Dast, financial advisor.\nParking is available behind the Musicians’ Center, with entrance on Bullion Street.\nReserve your parking spot with Clicknpark.\n\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCabaret-Théâtre du Vieux-Saint-Jean190 Rue Laurier, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC J3B 2K5\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45570_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Quartette in Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-quartette-in-saint-jean-sur-richelieu/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-12-4T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-12-4T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC_4021@prodKastallis-scaled-e1726693008557.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The four musicians of the <strong>Masmoudi Quartet</strong>, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity, and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long and rich tradition of Eastern music permeates each of Mohammed Masmoudi&#8217;s compositions with its modes and meters.</p> <p>With improvisations that borrow from both jazz and classical subtleties, sprinkled with klezmer inflections and tango rhythms, the works of the Masmoudi Quartet bear witness to the richness of a life that began in Tunisia and continued across the ocean, with a host of influences gathered along the way, in a spirit of genuine openness and experimentation.</p> <p><strong>Mohamed Masmoudi</strong> – oud<br /> <strong>Gabriel Paquin-Buki</strong> – clarinet<br /> <strong>Guillaume Martineau</strong> – piano<br /> <strong>Rémi-Jean LeBlanc</strong> – double bass</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Cabaret-Théâtre du Vieux-Saint-Jean\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"190 Rue Laurier, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC J3B 2K5\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Cabaret-Théâtre du Vieux-Saint-Jean\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu04dec18 h 00 min19 h 00 minMasmoudi Quartette in Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Cabaret-Théâtre du Vieux-Saint-Jean\n    Event DetailsThe four musicians of the Masmoudi Quartet, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity, and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The four musicians of the Masmoudi Quartet, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity, and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long and rich tradition of Eastern music permeates each of Mohammed Masmoudi’s compositions with its modes and meters.\nWith improvisations that borrow from both jazz and classical subtleties, sprinkled with klezmer inflections and tango rhythms, the works of the Masmoudi Quartet bear witness to the richness of a life that began in Tunisia and continued across the ocean, with a host of influences gathered along the way, in a spirit of genuine openness and experimentation.\nMohamed Masmoudi – oud\nGabriel Paquin-Buki – clarinet\nGuillaume Martineau – piano\nRémi-Jean LeBlanc – double bass\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCabaret-Théâtre du Vieux-Saint-Jean190 Rue Laurier, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC J3B 2K5Other Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45583_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Quartette in Lacombe\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-quartette-in-lacombe/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-12-4T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-12-4T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC_4021@prodKastallis-scaled-e1726693008557.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The four musicians of the <strong>Masmoudi Quartet</strong>, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity, and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long and rich tradition of Eastern music permeates each of Mohammed Masmoudi&#8217;s compositions with its modes and meters.</p> <p>With improvisations that borrow from both jazz and classical subtleties, sprinkled with klezmer inflections and tango rhythms, the works of the Masmoudi Quartet bear witness to the richness of a life that began in Tunisia and continued across the ocean, with a host of influences gathered along the way, in a spirit of genuine openness and experimentation.</p> <p><strong>Mohamed Masmoudi</strong> – oud<br /> <strong>Gabriel Paquin-Buki</strong> – clarinet<br /> <strong>Guillaume Martineau</strong> – piano<br /> <strong>Rémi-Jean LeBlanc</strong> – double bass</p> \",\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Burman University\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu04dec18 h 00 min19 h 00 minMasmoudi Quartette in Lacombe18 h 00 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Burman University\n    Event DetailsThe four musicians of the Masmoudi Quartet, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity, and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The four musicians of the Masmoudi Quartet, led by oud player Mohamed Masmoudi, are renowned for their versatility, sensitivity, and virtuosity. They present Villes Éternelles (2023), in which the long and rich tradition of Eastern music permeates each of Mohammed Masmoudi’s compositions with its modes and meters.\nWith improvisations that borrow from both jazz and classical subtleties, sprinkled with klezmer inflections and tango rhythms, the works of the Masmoudi Quartet bear witness to the richness of a life that began in Tunisia and continued across the ocean, with a host of influences gathered along the way, in a spirit of genuine openness and experimentation.\nMohamed Masmoudi – oud\nGabriel Paquin-Buki – clarinet\nGuillaume Martineau – piano\nRémi-Jean LeBlanc – double bass\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationBurman UniversityOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45860_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Ensembles and Choirs concert of the Centre des musiciens du monde\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/ensembles-and-choirs-concert/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-12-6T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-12-6T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Come see the <strong>students</strong> of the Centre des musiciens du monde perform!</div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Discover the sounds of the <strong>Balkans</strong>, <strong>Latin America</strong>, <strong>Eastern Europe</strong>, <strong>Middle East</strong>, and <strong>Turkey</strong>, and cheer on our students at their end-of-session concert.</div> <div></div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>December 6, 2025, 2 p.m. (doors open at 1:30 p.m.)<br class='html-br' />Access via the Saint-Enfant-Jésus church in Mile End</div> <div></div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Each ticket sold helps support the activities of the Center and its <strong>music school</strong>.</div> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat06dec14 h 00 min16 h 00 minEnsembles and Choirs concert of the Centre des musiciens du monde14 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsCome see the students of the Centre des musiciens du monde perform!\nDiscover the sounds of the Balkans, Latin America, Eastern    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Come see the students of the Centre des musiciens du monde perform!\nDiscover the sounds of the Balkans, Latin America, Eastern Europe, Middle East, and Turkey, and cheer on our students at their end-of-session concert.\n\nDecember 6, 2025, 2 p.m. (doors open at 1:30 p.m.)Access via the Saint-Enfant-Jésus church in Mile End\n\nEach ticket sold helps support the activities of the Center and its music school.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44524_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Didem Başar – Under the moon of Topkapı\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/didem-basar-under-the-moon-of-topkapi/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2025-12-17T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2025-12-17T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CONCERT-2.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>By plucking the multiple strings of her <strong>kanun</strong>, Turkey&#8217;s large zither, <strong>Didem Başar</strong> opens the doors to a world of crystal-clear sound. Heir to a centuries-old tradition, she makes her 78 strings sing with a finesse and emotion that transcend time.<br /> Her repertoire, drawn from the sources of Turkish music, unfolds melodies with subtle inflections, where each note seems to carry the scent of Istanbul and the memory of its shores, like a moonlit reflection on the waters of the Bosphorus.</p> <p>Between virtuosity and delicacy, her interpretations weave a living link between past and present, inviting the listener on a journey where ancient resonances dialogue with today&#8217;s sensibilities.</p> <p><strong>Artist :</strong><br /> Didem Başar : kanun</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed17dec19 h 30 min20 h 30 minDidem Başar – Under the moon of TopkapıConcert intime19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsBy plucking the multiple strings of her kanun, Turkey’s large zither, Didem Başar opens the doors to a world of crystal-clear sound. Heir to a centuries-old tradition, she makes her    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                By plucking the multiple strings of her kanun, Turkey’s large zither, Didem Başar opens the doors to a world of crystal-clear sound. Heir to a centuries-old tradition, she makes her 78 strings sing with a finesse and emotion that transcend time.\nHer repertoire, drawn from the sources of Turkish music, unfolds melodies with subtle inflections, where each note seems to carry the scent of Istanbul and the memory of its shores, like a moonlit reflection on the waters of the Bosphorus.\nBetween virtuosity and delicacy, her interpretations weave a living link between past and present, inviting the listener on a journey where ancient resonances dialogue with today’s sensibilities.\nArtist :\nDidem Başar : kanun\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_46500_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Cajón workshop - Bossa-nova\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/cajon-workshop-bossa-nova/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-1-15T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-1-29T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Atelier-cajon-bossa.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>A versatile instrument par excellence, the <strong>cajón</strong> can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.</p> <p>This winter, join us for a series of intensive <strong>cajón workshops</strong> specially designed to teach you <strong>how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón</strong>.<br /> In three 1.5-hour sessions, you will learn to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of <strong>bossa nova</strong>.</p> <p>We will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.</p> <p>Thursdays, January 15, 22, and 29.</p> <p><em>Upcoming workshops: </em><br /> <em>Spanish rumba: February 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</em><br /> <em>Funk-pop: March 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</em></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu15jan(jan 15)18 h 00 minthu29(jan 29)19 h 30 minCajón workshop - Bossa-nova18 h 00 min - 19 h 30 min (29)(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsA versatile instrument par excellence, the cajón can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.\nThis winter, join us for    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                A versatile instrument par excellence, the cajón can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.\nThis winter, join us for a series of intensive cajón workshops specially designed to teach you how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón.\nIn three 1.5-hour sessions, you will learn to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of bossa nova.\nWe will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.\nThursdays, January 15, 22, and 29.\nUpcoming workshops: \nSpanish rumba: February 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\nFunk-pop: March 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44532_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Echoes of Sakartvelo - Georgian Polyphonies\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/echoes-of-sakartvelo-georgian-polyphonies/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-1-23T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-1-23T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ori-Shalva-Echos-complet-1.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>SOLD OUT<br /> Georgian polyphony</strong> is one of the oldest and most complex of singing traditions. Family singing plays an essential role, having enabled it to survive through centuries of invasions and occupations.<br /> For <strong>Ori Shlava</strong> (Shalva Makharashvili, Andrea Kuzmich and their sons Shalva-Lucas and Gabo), singing is as natural as breathing, rooted in family celebrations rather than stage performances.</p> <p>The authenticity of their music stems from years of dedication and a musical heritage handed down from generation to generation.</p> <p><strong>Artists :</strong><br /> Shalva Makharashvili : singer<br /> Andrea Kuzmich : singer<br /> Shalva-Lucas : singer<br /> Gabo : singer</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri23jan19 h 30 min20 h 30 minEchoes of Sakartvelo - Georgian PolyphoniesConcert intime19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsSOLD OUT\nGeorgian polyphony is one of the oldest and most complex of singing traditions. Family singing plays an essential role, having enabled it to survive through centuries of invasions    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                SOLD OUT\nGeorgian polyphony is one of the oldest and most complex of singing traditions. Family singing plays an essential role, having enabled it to survive through centuries of invasions and occupations.\nFor Ori Shlava (Shalva Makharashvili, Andrea Kuzmich and their sons Shalva-Lucas and Gabo), singing is as natural as breathing, rooted in family celebrations rather than stage performances.\nThe authenticity of their music stems from years of dedication and a musical heritage handed down from generation to generation.\nArtists :\nShalva Makharashvili : singer\nAndrea Kuzmich : singer\nShalva-Lucas : singer\nGabo : singer\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_45963_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Workshop - Georgian polyphonies\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/workshop-georgian-polyphonies/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-1-24T10:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-1-24T17:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Stage-Ori-Shalva-H26.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>You are invited to a day-long singing workshop with the Georgian ensemble<strong> Ori Shalva</strong>.</p> <p>Take part in a <strong>Georgian singing</strong> workshop and join the thousands of voices that have perpetuated this thousand-year-old folk tradition, recognized by UNESCO as a masterpiece of intangible cultural heritage. Rooted in the Caucasus, at the crossroads of Europe and Asia, Georgian polyphony is renowned for its haunting harmonies and rich regional diversity, defying Western musical conventions.</p> <p>During this one-day workshop, we will explore songs from across Georgia, from lively travel and toast songs to Christmas carols and meditative chants. Lyrics (and sometimes sheet music) will be provided, but songs will mainly be taught by ear in order to better convey the subtle musical nuances of this tradition. We will also work on vocal techniques characteristic of Georgia and situate the songs in their cultural and historical context. If time and energy permit, we may even learn a traditional circle dance, combining song and movement.</p> <p>Ori Shalva, also known as the “Makharashvili Family,” is one of the few professional ensembles in the Georgian diaspora. The members of this Toronto-based ensemble are Shalva, a singer and traditional Georgian instrumentalist; Andrea, a professional singer and leading figure in Georgian singing ethnomusicology; and their son, Shalva-Lucas. The group has been offering workshops to polyphony enthusiasts for 20 years.</p> <p>No knowledge of Georgian is required; singers must be comfortable singing in harmony and eager to learn.</p> <p>For a glimpse of Georgian singing: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b4aJMFpA8kg&amp;t=9s</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat24jan10 h 00 min17 h 00 minWorkshop - Georgian polyphonies10 h 00 min - 17 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsYou are invited to a day-long singing workshop with the Georgian ensemble Ori Shalva.\nTake part in a Georgian singing workshop and join the thousands of voices that have perpetuated this    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                You are invited to a day-long singing workshop with the Georgian ensemble Ori Shalva.\nTake part in a Georgian singing workshop and join the thousands of voices that have perpetuated this thousand-year-old folk tradition, recognized by UNESCO as a masterpiece of intangible cultural heritage. Rooted in the Caucasus, at the crossroads of Europe and Asia, Georgian polyphony is renowned for its haunting harmonies and rich regional diversity, defying Western musical conventions.\nDuring this one-day workshop, we will explore songs from across Georgia, from lively travel and toast songs to Christmas carols and meditative chants. Lyrics (and sometimes sheet music) will be provided, but songs will mainly be taught by ear in order to better convey the subtle musical nuances of this tradition. We will also work on vocal techniques characteristic of Georgia and situate the songs in their cultural and historical context. If time and energy permit, we may even learn a traditional circle dance, combining song and movement.\nOri Shalva, also known as the “Makharashvili Family,” is one of the few professional ensembles in the Georgian diaspora. The members of this Toronto-based ensemble are Shalva, a singer and traditional Georgian instrumentalist; Andrea, a professional singer and leading figure in Georgian singing ethnomusicology; and their son, Shalva-Lucas. The group has been offering workshops to polyphony enthusiasts for 20 years.\nNo knowledge of Georgian is required; singers must be comfortable singing in harmony and eager to learn.\nFor a glimpse of Georgian singing: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b4aJMFpA8kg&t=9s\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges5290 Chemin de la Côte-des-Neiges Montréal, QC H3T 1Y2\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_46975_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Siraba in Côte des Neiges\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/siraba-in-cote-des-neiges/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-1T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-1T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/2023_11_27_ADAMA-DAOU16745-copie-scaled-e1727542495185.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p><strong>Siraba</strong> means “the great path,” a proposal for dialogue between three continents&#8230;<br /> Attend a concert featuring the renewed ancient traditions of <strong>Mali</strong>, <strong>West Africa</strong>, <strong>South America</strong>, and <strong>Europe</strong>!</p> <p><strong>Artists:</strong><br /> Adama Daou: balafon;<br /> Gabriel Schwartz: flute, pandeiro;<br /> Aboulaye Koné: electric guitar;<br /> Christian Obam: electric bass.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5290 Chemin de la Côte-des-Neiges Montréal, QC H3T 1Y2\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Maison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun01feb15 h 00 min16 h 00 minSiraba in Côte des Neiges15 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Maison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges\n    Event DetailsSiraba means “the great path,” a proposal for dialogue between three continents…\nAttend a concert featuring the renewed ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America, and Europe!\nArtists:\nAdama Daou:    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Siraba means “the great path,” a proposal for dialogue between three continents…\nAttend a concert featuring the renewed ancient traditions of Mali, West Africa, South America, and Europe!\nArtists:\nAdama Daou: balafon;\nGabriel Schwartz: flute, pandeiro;\nAboulaye Koné: electric guitar;\nChristian Obam: electric bass.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison de la culture de Côte-des-Neiges5290 Chemin de la Côte-des-Neiges Montréal, QC H3T 1Y2Other Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44570_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"A Night in the Garden of Eden\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/a-night-in-the-garden-of-eden/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-11T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-11T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CONCERT-4.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>With<em><strong> A Night in the Garden of Eden</strong></em>  pianist <strong>Guillaume Martineau</strong> and clarinetist <strong>Gabriel Paquin-Buki</strong> take us on a journey where musical boundaries fade away. Their duo navigates with ease between the refinement of classical music and the warmth of folklore, punctuating their dialogue with jazz improvisations and original compositions.</p> <p>The vibrant roots of <strong>klezmer</strong> mingle with the enchanting scents of the Mediterranean coast, while bursts of Latin rhythms dance across the lands of romantic Europe.</p> <p><strong>Artists:</strong><br /> Guillaume Martineau: piano<br /> Gabriel Paquin-Buki: clarinet<strong><br /> </strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed11feb19 h 30 min20 h 30 minA Night in the Garden of EdenConcert intime19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsWith A Night in the Garden of Eden  pianist Guillaume Martineau and clarinetist Gabriel Paquin-Buki take us on a journey where musical boundaries fade away. Their duo navigates with ease    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                With A Night in the Garden of Eden  pianist Guillaume Martineau and clarinetist Gabriel Paquin-Buki take us on a journey where musical boundaries fade away. Their duo navigates with ease between the refinement of classical music and the warmth of folklore, punctuating their dialogue with jazz improvisations and original compositions.\nThe vibrant roots of klezmer mingle with the enchanting scents of the Mediterranean coast, while bursts of Latin rhythms dance across the lands of romantic Europe.\nArtists:\nGuillaume Martineau: piano\nGabriel Paquin-Buki: clarinet\n\n \n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_46510_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Cajón workshop - Spanish rumba\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/cajon-workshop-spanish-rumba/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-11T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-25T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/atelier-cajon-rumba.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>A versatile instrument par excellence, the <strong>cajón</strong> can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.</p> <p>This winter, join us for a series of intensive <strong>cajón workshops</strong> specially designed to teach you <strong>how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón</strong>.<br /> In three 1.5-hour sessions, you will learn to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of <strong>Spanish rumba</strong>.</p> <p>We will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.</p> <p>Wednesdays, February 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</p> <p><em>Upcoming workshops: </em><br /> <em>Funk-pop: March 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</em></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed11feb(feb 11)18 h 00 minwed25(feb 25)19 h 30 minCajón workshop - Spanish rumba18 h 00 min - 19 h 30 min (25)(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsA versatile instrument par excellence, the cajón can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.\nThis winter, join us for    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                A versatile instrument par excellence, the cajón can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.\nThis winter, join us for a series of intensive cajón workshops specially designed to teach you how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón.\nIn three 1.5-hour sessions, you will learn to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of Spanish rumba.\nWe will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.\nWednesdays, February 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\nUpcoming workshops: \nFunk-pop: March 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47046_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Andalusyria in Mauricie - CANCELLED\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/andalusyria-in-mauricie/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-13T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-13T21:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/CA_9811-scaled-e1726788739905.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>This event is unfortunatly cancelled.</p> <p><strong>Andalusyria</strong> brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of <strong>flamenco and Arabic traditions</strong>.<br /> <strong>Nazih Borish</strong>, a musician based in Montreal, is a self-taught oud virtuoso who founded his own music school in his hometown of Lattakia, Syria.<br /> <strong>Gabriel Evangelista</strong>, a Montrealer of Spanish origin, is a flamenco-jazz pianist. Both have developed their own musical language throughout their careers and are committed to this artistic encounter that links their cultural and personal horizons.<br /> The result: great poetry built on flights of improvised notes, unique from one performance to the next.</p> \",\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Gîte Comme un Accord\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri13feb19 h 30 min21 h 00 minAndalusyria in Mauricie - CANCELLED19 h 30 min - 21 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Gîte Comme un Accord\n    Event DetailsThis event is unfortunatly cancelled.\nAndalusyria brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arabic traditions.\nNazih Borish, a musician based in    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                This event is unfortunatly cancelled.\nAndalusyria brings together two talented artists who have created an original repertoire at the crossroads of flamenco and Arabic traditions.\nNazih Borish, a musician based in Montreal, is a self-taught oud virtuoso who founded his own music school in his hometown of Lattakia, Syria.\nGabriel Evangelista, a Montrealer of Spanish origin, is a flamenco-jazz pianist. Both have developed their own musical language throughout their careers and are committed to this artistic encounter that links their cultural and personal horizons.\nThe result: great poetry built on flights of improvised notes, unique from one performance to the next.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationGîte Comme un AccordOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_46682_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Renaissance dance workshop\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/renaissance-dance-workshop/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-14T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-14T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/495x400-Danses-Renaissance-140225.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Discover the steps and figures of historical <strong>Renaissance dances</strong> repertoires, a lavish period of Italian and French courts in the 15th and 16th centuries, in this first monthly workshop of a series of four.</p> <p>On the program for this workshop with <strong>Anne-Marie Gardette</strong>: Spagnoletta by Caroso (Il Ballarino, Venice, 1581), Bassa danza Cupido by Guglielmo Ebreo (Ms, 1463), the ballroom dances from Thoinot Arbeau&#8217;s Orchésographie, pavane and gaillarde, common and cut branles (round dances) including the Branle des chevaux and the Branle de la guerre. We will also dance the dance of the Bouffons (sword dance).</p> <p>Open to all.</p> <p>Upcoming workshops:<br /> March 14, April 4, and May 2<br /> From 2:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m.</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat14feb14 h 00 min16 h 00 minRenaissance dance workshop14 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsDiscover the steps and figures of historical Renaissance dances repertoires, a lavish period of Italian and French courts in the 15th and 16th centuries, in this first monthly workshop of    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Discover the steps and figures of historical Renaissance dances repertoires, a lavish period of Italian and French courts in the 15th and 16th centuries, in this first monthly workshop of a series of four.\nOn the program for this workshop with Anne-Marie Gardette: Spagnoletta by Caroso (Il Ballarino, Venice, 1581), Bassa danza Cupido by Guglielmo Ebreo (Ms, 1463), the ballroom dances from Thoinot Arbeau’s Orchésographie, pavane and gaillarde, common and cut branles (round dances) including the Branle des chevaux and the Branle de la guerre. We will also dance the dance of the Bouffons (sword dance).\nOpen to all.\nUpcoming workshops:\nMarch 14, April 4, and May 2\nFrom 2:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47077_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Workshop - Classical Arabic singing\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/worshop-classical-arabic-singing/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-19T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-21T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/273x195-lamia.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Join<strong> Lamia Yared</strong> for three immersive evenings dedicated to the <em>maqams</em> of Arabic music, explored through the refined repertoire of <em>muwashahat</em>.<br /> During this <strong>intensive workshop</strong> in <strong>classical Arabic singing</strong>, you will discover their characteristic intervals and rhythms, while learning the essential basics of Oriental singing technique and interpretation.</p> <p>An ideal format for refining your ear, voice, and musicality!</p> <p>February 19 and 20 from 6 to 8 pm and February 21 from 3 to 5 pm</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu19feb(feb 19)18 h 00 minsat21(feb 21)20 h 00 minWorkshop - Classical Arabic singing18 h 00 min - 20 h 00 min (21)(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsJoin Lamia Yared for three immersive evenings dedicated to the maqams of Arabic music, explored through the refined repertoire of muwashahat.\nDuring this intensive workshop in classical Arabic singing, you    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Join Lamia Yared for three immersive evenings dedicated to the maqams of Arabic music, explored through the refined repertoire of muwashahat.\nDuring this intensive workshop in classical Arabic singing, you will discover their characteristic intervals and rhythms, while learning the essential basics of Oriental singing technique and interpretation.\nAn ideal format for refining your ear, voice, and musicality!\nFebruary 19 and 20 from 6 to 8 pm and February 21 from 3 to 5 pm\n \n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tThéâtre Alphonse-Desjardins25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47041_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"SYMBIOSE\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/symbiose-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-21T20:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-21T21:15-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Creation-sans-titre-8.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Would you like to listen to the vocal melodies of <strong>Cameroon</strong>&#8216;s forests against a backdrop of Italian music and Latin rhythms?<br /> The <strong>Café Korigé</strong> trio will be at the Alphonse-Desjardins Theater in Repentigny on February 21.</p> <p>Artists:<br /> <strong>Geremia Lodi</strong>: flute, vocals, body percussion<br /> <strong>Komty Ondoua</strong>: vocals<br /> <strong>Ricardo Soriano</strong>: piano, cajón, bongos, violin</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Aramusique\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat21feb20 h 00 min21 h 15 minSYMBIOSE20 h 00 min - 21 h 15 min(GMT-05:00) Théâtre Alphonse-Desjardins\n    Event DetailsWould you like to listen to the vocal melodies of Cameroon‘s forests against a backdrop of Italian music and Latin rhythms?\nThe Café Korigé trio will be at the Alphonse-Desjardins    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Would you like to listen to the vocal melodies of Cameroon‘s forests against a backdrop of Italian music and Latin rhythms?\nThe Café Korigé trio will be at the Alphonse-Desjardins Theater in Repentigny on February 21.\nArtists:\nGeremia Lodi: flute, vocals, body percussion\nKomty Ondoua: vocals\nRicardo Soriano: piano, cajón, bongos, violin\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationThéâtre Alphonse-Desjardins25 All. de la Création, Repentigny, QC J6A 0C2Other Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47050_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Silk Notebooks: Echoes from East to West in Ville Saint-Laurent\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/silk-notebooks-echoes-from-east-to-west-in-ville-saint-laurent/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-22T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-22T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/19_jun_CMM_jmalobaton_-13-e1725711929972.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>In their musical encounter, musicians <strong>Ran Wang</strong> (guzheng) and <strong>Annette Bauer</strong> (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor) travel the <strong>Silk Road from east to west</strong>.</p> <p><strong>Pre-concert talk led by music mediator Frédéric Cardin from 1:15 p.m. to 1:45 p.m.</strong></p> <p>Their journey invites the audience to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, also weaving links between different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC–9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.<br /> The program is also inspired by the different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveler might encounter—from observing deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveler might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments and the multiple vibrations of their strings, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.</p> \",\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des loisirs de Saint-Laurent\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun22feb14 h 00 min15 h 00 minSilk Notebooks: Echoes from East to West in Ville Saint-Laurent14 h 00 min - 15 h 00 min(GMT-05:00) Centre des loisirs de Saint-Laurent\n    Event DetailsIn their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor) travel the Silk Road from east to west.\nPre-concert talk led by music mediator Frédéric Cardin    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang (guzheng) and Annette Bauer (sarode, recorders, duduk, tabor) travel the Silk Road from east to west.\nPre-concert talk led by music mediator Frédéric Cardin from 1:15 p.m. to 1:45 p.m.\nTheir journey invites the audience to follow a geographical route from China to Italy via India, also weaving links between different historical periods by presenting music from the ancient Han dynasty (200 BC–9 AD) to music from the nascent European Renaissance in early 15th-century Italy.\nThe program is also inspired by the different physical and emotional landscapes that an imaginary traveler might encounter—from observing deeply moving beauty in unfamiliar landscapes to the audacity of a long journey, to the loneliness a traveler might feel far from home. Above all, their musical journey is a conversation between the sounds of their instruments and the multiple vibrations of their strings, leaving room for improvisation and exploration of the unknown.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des loisirs de Saint-LaurentOther Events\n\t\t\n\tThe Bassment202 4th Ave N Saskatoon, SK S7K 0K1\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47148_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Quartette in Saskatoon\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-quartette-in-saskatoon/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-26T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-26T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC_4163-copy-scaled-e1726693312605.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>When cultures meet in the music of the <strong>Masmoudi Quartet</strong>, the result is truly extraordinary. Jazz is enriched by the interaction between Western and Middle Eastern instruments to create a tapestry of sound that is both familiar and unexpected. The group&#8217;s leader, <strong>Mohamed Masmoudi</strong>, is originally from Tunisia, and his music incorporates influences from a life devoted to study, travel, and performance. His works are known for their melodic richness and multifaceted texture. A sample of Masmoudi&#8217;s repertoire is a journey through moods and landscapes, from the lively Labyrinth to the sensual Moorish Tango.</p> <p>Audiences will be intrigued by this unique mosaic of classical, jazz, and world music.</p> <p>Artists:<br /> <strong>Mohamed Masmoudi</strong>: oud<br /> <strong>Guillame Martineau</strong>: piano<br /> <strong>Gabriel Paquin-Buki</strong>: clarinet<br /> <strong>Rémi-Jean Leblanc:</strong> double bass.</p> <p><em>Presented by the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra and the Saskatoon Jazz Society.</em></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"The Bassment\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"202 4th Ave N Saskatoon, SK S7K 0K1\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu26feb19 h 30 min20 h 30 minMasmoudi Quartette in Saskatoon19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT-05:00) The Bassment\n    Event DetailsWhen cultures meet in the music of the Masmoudi Quartet, the result is truly extraordinary. Jazz is enriched by the interaction between Western and Middle Eastern instruments to create a    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                When cultures meet in the music of the Masmoudi Quartet, the result is truly extraordinary. Jazz is enriched by the interaction between Western and Middle Eastern instruments to create a tapestry of sound that is both familiar and unexpected. The group’s leader, Mohamed Masmoudi, is originally from Tunisia, and his music incorporates influences from a life devoted to study, travel, and performance. His works are known for their melodic richness and multifaceted texture. A sample of Masmoudi’s repertoire is a journey through moods and landscapes, from the lively Labyrinth to the sensual Moorish Tango.\nAudiences will be intrigued by this unique mosaic of classical, jazz, and world music.\nArtists:\nMohamed Masmoudi: oud\nGuillame Martineau: piano\nGabriel Paquin-Buki: clarinet\nRémi-Jean Leblanc: double bass.\nPresented by the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra and the Saskatoon Jazz Society.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationThe Bassment202 4th Ave N Saskatoon, SK S7K 0K1Other Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47090_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"February traditional song veillée\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/february-traditional-song-veillee/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-27T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-27T22:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/273x195-veillee.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Every last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of <strong>traditional songs</strong> from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!<br /> Regulars, newcomers, and accompanying musicians are all welcome!</p> <p>The veillée is hosted by <strong>Lysandre Chartrand</strong>.</p> <p>Fridays, February 27, March 27, April 24, and May 29, 2026, from 7:30 pm to 10:30 pm<br /> Cost: $10 (cash only)</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Lysandre Chartrand\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri27feb19 h 30 min22 h 30 minFebruary traditional song veillée19 h 30 min - 22 h 30 min(GMT-05:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsEvery last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of traditional songs from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!\nRegulars, newcomers,    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Every last Friday of the month, come share, listen, or simply discover a repertoire of traditional songs from here and elsewhere starting at 7:30 pm with a veillée!\nRegulars, newcomers, and accompanying musicians are all welcome!\nThe veillée is hosted by Lysandre Chartrand.\nFridays, February 27, March 27, April 24, and May 29, 2026, from 7:30 pm to 10:30 pm\nCost: $10 (cash only)\n \n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47156_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Masmoudi Quartette in Canmore\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/masmoudi-quartette-in-canmore/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-2-28T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-2-28T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DSC_4163-copy-scaled-e1726693312605.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>When cultures meet in the music of the <strong>Masmoudi Quartet</strong>, the result is truly extraordinary. <strong>Jazz</strong> is enriched by the interaction between Western and Middle Eastern instruments to create a tapestry of sound that is both familiar and unexpected. The group&#8217;s leader, <strong>Mohamed Masmoudi</strong>, is originally from Tunisia, and his music incorporates influences from a life devoted to study, travel, and performance. His works are known for their melodic richness and multifaceted texture. A sample of Masmoudi&#8217;s repertoire is a journey through moods and landscapes, from the lively Labyrinth to the sensual Moorish Tango.</p> <p>Artists:<br /> <strong>Mohamed Masmoudi</strong>: oud<br /> <strong>Guillame Martineau</strong>: piano<br /> <strong>Gabriel Paquin-Buki</strong>: clarinet<br /> <strong>Rémi-Jean Leblanc</strong>: double bass.</p> \",\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Arts Place Canmore\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat28feb19 h 30 min20 h 30 minMasmoudi Quartette in Canmore19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT-05:00) Arts Place Canmore\n    Event DetailsWhen cultures meet in the music of the Masmoudi Quartet, the result is truly extraordinary. Jazz is enriched by the interaction between Western and Middle Eastern instruments to create a    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                When cultures meet in the music of the Masmoudi Quartet, the result is truly extraordinary. Jazz is enriched by the interaction between Western and Middle Eastern instruments to create a tapestry of sound that is both familiar and unexpected. The group’s leader, Mohamed Masmoudi, is originally from Tunisia, and his music incorporates influences from a life devoted to study, travel, and performance. His works are known for their melodic richness and multifaceted texture. A sample of Masmoudi’s repertoire is a journey through moods and landscapes, from the lively Labyrinth to the sensual Moorish Tango.\nArtists:\nMohamed Masmoudi: oud\nGuillame Martineau: piano\nGabriel Paquin-Buki: clarinet\nRémi-Jean Leblanc: double bass.\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationArts Place CanmoreOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47291_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Renaissance Dances Workshop – March\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/renaissance-dances-workshop-march/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-3-14T14:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-3-14T16:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Danses-R-mars.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>The <strong>Renaissance</strong> was an important period for the development of <strong>dance</strong> in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.</p> <p>This series of<strong> workshops</strong> offered by <strong>Anne-Marie Gardette</strong> will focus on the dances of the Italian courts of the Quattrocento and Cinquecento (bassa danza, balletto, etc.). The ball repertoire in use in France at the end of the 16th century, according to Thoinot Arbeau&#8217;s essential Orchésographie (branle, pavane, gaillarde, etc.), will also be covered.<br /> These two-hour workshops are open to all, and musicians who play this repertoire (Praetorius, Attaingnant, Gervaise, Phalèse, etc.) and want to learn about the dances are also welcome.</p> <p>Each workshop will cover different dances, so they can be taken independently.<br /> Open to all.<br /> Upcoming workshops:<br /> April 11 and May 2<br /> From 2:00 pm to 4:00 pm</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tsat14mar14 h 00 min16 h 00 minRenaissance Dances Workshop – March14 h 00 min - 16 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsThe Renaissance was an important period for the development of dance in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.\nThis series of workshops offered by    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                The Renaissance was an important period for the development of dance in the West, as it saw the emergence of the very first dance treatises.\nThis series of workshops offered by Anne-Marie Gardette will focus on the dances of the Italian courts of the Quattrocento and Cinquecento (bassa danza, balletto, etc.). The ball repertoire in use in France at the end of the 16th century, according to Thoinot Arbeau’s essential Orchésographie (branle, pavane, gaillarde, etc.), will also be covered.\nThese two-hour workshops are open to all, and musicians who play this repertoire (Praetorius, Attaingnant, Gervaise, Phalèse, etc.) and want to learn about the dances are also welcome.\nEach workshop will cover different dances, so they can be taken independently.\nOpen to all.\nUpcoming workshops:\nApril 11 and May 2\nFrom 2:00 pm to 4:00 pm\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_44577_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"The Sparkle of Inner Strings\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/the-sparkle-of-inner-strings/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-3-18T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-3-18T20:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/CONCERT-5.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>In this solo <strong>santur</strong> (Persian zither) concert, the music flows between improvisations and original compositions by artist <strong>Sadaf Amini.<br /> </strong> The pieces selected for this evening are based on years of rhythmic and melodic immersion, conveying a range of emotions centered on joy and sadness, and their subtle transformations.</p> <p>The journey moves from classically inspired structures to rhythms and melodies interwoven with abstract layers of sound in perpetual development.</p> <p><strong>Artist:</strong><br /> Sadaf Amini: santur</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5039 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed18mar19 h 30 min20 h 30 minThe Sparkle of Inner StringsConcert intime19 h 30 min - 20 h 30 min(GMT+00:00) Saint-Enfant-Jesus Church\n    Event DetailsIn this solo santur (Persian zither) concert, the music flows between improvisations and original compositions by artist Sadaf Amini.\n The pieces selected for this evening are based on years    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                In this solo santur (Persian zither) concert, the music flows between improvisations and original compositions by artist Sadaf Amini.\n The pieces selected for this evening are based on years of rhythmic and melodic immersion, conveying a range of emotions centered on joy and sadness, and their subtle transformations.\nThe journey moves from classically inspired structures to rhythms and melodies interwoven with abstract layers of sound in perpetual development.\nArtist:\nSadaf Amini: santur\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tTicket officeI reserve my place\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationSaint-Enfant-Jesus Church5039 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47366_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Persian evening\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/persian-evening/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-3-18T17:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-3-18T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/evenement-Nuit-persane.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Are you a musician? Before the Persian music concert featuring Sadaf Amini, bring your instrument to celebrate the Iranian New Year, Nowruz, and discover the Center&#8217;s Persian music ensemble, led by gheychak player Reza Abaee.<br /> Tea, snacks, and fruit will be served on site.<br /> Join the ensemble for an evening!</p> <p>Prerequisite: play an instrument capable of producing quarter tones.</p> <p>From 5:30 pm to 7 pm<br /> Free admission<br /> Centre des musiciens du monde<br /> 5043 Saint-Dominique Street, Montreal<br /> Rooms 203 and 204</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed18mar17 h 30 min19 h 00 minPersian evening17 h 30 min - 19 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsAre you a musician? Before the Persian music concert featuring Sadaf Amini, bring your instrument to celebrate the Iranian New Year, Nowruz, and discover the Center’s Persian music ensemble, led    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Are you a musician? Before the Persian music concert featuring Sadaf Amini, bring your instrument to celebrate the Iranian New Year, Nowruz, and discover the Center’s Persian music ensemble, led by gheychak player Reza Abaee.\nTea, snacks, and fruit will be served on site.\nJoin the ensemble for an evening!\nPrerequisite: play an instrument capable of producing quarter tones.\nFrom 5:30 pm to 7 pm\nFree admission\nCentre des musiciens du monde\n5043 Saint-Dominique Street, Montreal\nRooms 203 and 204\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_46517_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Cajón workshop - Funk pop\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/cajon-workshop-funk-pop/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-3-18T18:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-4-1T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/stage-cajon-funk-pop.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>A versatile instrument par excellence, the <strong>cajón</strong> can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.</p> <p>This winter, join us for a series of intensive <strong>cajón workshops</strong> specially designed to teach you <strong>how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón</strong>.<br /> In three 1.5-hour sessions, you will be able to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of <strong>funk-pop</strong>.</p> <p>We will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.</p> <p>Wednesdays, March 18, 25 and April 1st</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\"}]}\n\t\t\t\twed18marwed01aprCajón workshop - Funk pop(March 18) 18 h 00 min - (April 1) 19 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsA versatile instrument par excellence, the cajón can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.\nThis winter, join us for    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                A versatile instrument par excellence, the cajón can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.\nThis winter, join us for a series of intensive cajón workshops specially designed to teach you how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón.\nIn three 1.5-hour sessions, you will be able to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of funk-pop.\nWe will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.\nWednesdays, March 18, 25 and April 1st\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tMaison Brignon-Dit-Lapierre4251, boulevard Gouin Est Montréal (Québec) H1H 5L9{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47444_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Carnet de soie : échos d&#039;est en ouest\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/carnet-de-soie-echos-dest-en-ouest-2/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-3-19T19:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-3-19T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/19_jun_CMM_jmalobaton_-13-e1725711929972.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>A musical journey along the Silk Road, between China, India, and Italy. With guzheng, sarod, flutes, dubuk, and tabor, the musicians travel through time.</p> <p>From the Han Dynasty to the Renaissance, guided by an imaginary traveler, they discover unfamiliar landscapes, beauty, and solitude. A performance presented by the World Musicians Center.</p> <p><strong>Musicians : </strong>Ran Wang, <em>ghuzeng </em>| Annette Bauer, <em>sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor</em></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Maison Brignon-Dit-Lapierre\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"4251, boulevard Gouin Est Montréal (Québec) H1H 5L9\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tthu19mar19 h 00 minCarnet de soie : échos d'est en ouest19 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Maison Brignon-Dit-Lapierre\n    Event DetailsA musical journey along the Silk Road, between China, India, and Italy. With guzheng, sarod, flutes, dubuk, and tabor, the musicians travel through time.\nFrom the Han Dynasty to the Renaissance,    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                A musical journey along the Silk Road, between China, India, and Italy. With guzheng, sarod, flutes, dubuk, and tabor, the musicians travel through time.\nFrom the Han Dynasty to the Renaissance, guided by an imaginary traveler, they discover unfamiliar landscapes, beauty, and solitude. A performance presented by the World Musicians Center.\nMusicians : Ran Wang, ghuzeng | Annette Bauer, sarod, recorders, duduk, pipe and tabor\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationMaison Brignon-Dit-Lapierre4251, boulevard Gouin Est Montréal (Québec) H1H 5L9Other Events\n\t\t\n\tCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique Street\n\t\t\t\t    \t{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47109_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Traditional songs from French-speaking America Veillée\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/traditional-songs-from-french-speaking-america-veillee/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-3-27T19:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-3-27T22:30-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/273x195-veillee.png\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>On <strong>Quebec&#8217;s Canadian Francophonie Day</strong>, the Centre des musiciens du monde invites Montrealers to a <strong>traditional songs from French-speaking America Veillée</strong>, hosted by <strong>Lysandre Chartrand</strong>, on March 27, 2026, in Montreal from 7:30 p.m. to 11 p.m.<br /> Come share, listen, and connect over the French-language song repertoires of <strong>Quebec</strong>, <strong>Acadia</strong>, <strong>Ontario</strong>, and the <strong>Prairies</strong>.</p> <p>Admission: $10 (cash only)</p> <p><em>This project is made possible thanks to the financial support of the Government of Quebec, under its programs supporting the Canadian Francophonie.</em></p> <p><a href='https://www.quebec.ca/gouvernement/politiques-orientations/langue-francaise/francophonie-canadienne'><img class='alignnone size-full wp-image-47110' src='https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/QUEBEC_w3_COUL_ParticipFinanc-1.png' alt='' width='199' height='72' /></a></p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Centre des musiciens du monde\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"5043 Saint-Dominique Street\"}}],\"organizer\":[{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Lysandre Chartrand\"}]}\n\t\t\t\tfri27mar19 h 30 min22 h 30 minTraditional songs from French-speaking America Veillée19 h 30 min - 22 h 30 min(GMT-04:00) Centre des musiciens du monde\n    Event DetailsOn Quebec’s Canadian Francophonie Day, the Centre des musiciens du monde invites Montrealers to a traditional songs from French-speaking America Veillée, hosted by Lysandre Chartrand, on March 27, 2026, in    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                On Quebec’s Canadian Francophonie Day, the Centre des musiciens du monde invites Montrealers to a traditional songs from French-speaking America Veillée, hosted by Lysandre Chartrand, on March 27, 2026, in Montreal from 7:30 p.m. to 11 p.m.\nCome share, listen, and connect over the French-language song repertoires of Quebec, Acadia, Ontario, and the Prairies.\nAdmission: $10 (cash only)\nThis project is made possible thanks to the financial support of the Government of Quebec, under its programs supporting the Canadian Francophonie.\n\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationCentre des musiciens du monde5043 Saint-Dominique StreetOther Events\n\t\t\n\tÉglise Saint-Édouard6500 Rue de Saint-Vallier, Montréal, QC H2S 2P7{\"@context\": \"http://schema.org\",\"@type\": \"Event\",\n\t\t\t\t\"@id\": \"event_47468_0\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventAttendanceMode\":\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n\t\t\t\t\"eventStatus\":\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n\t\t\t\t\"name\": \"Carnets de soie : Échos d’est en ouest\",\n\t\t\t\t\"url\": \"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/carnets-de-soie-echos-dest-en-ouest-5/var/ri-0.l-L2\",\n\t\t\t\t\"startDate\": \"2026-3-29T15:00-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"endDate\": \"2026-3-29T23:59-4:00\",\n\t\t\t\t\"image\":\"https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/19_jun_CMM_jmalobaton_-13-e1725711929972.jpg\", \n\t\t\t\t\"description\":\"<p>Come and experience this musical performance that journeys along the Silk Road from East to West.</p> <p>In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang and Annette Bauer travel the Silk Road, from China to Italy via India. Their journey weaves together the music of the ancient Han Dynasty with that of the European Renaissance in a dialogue between their instruments: the guzheng, the sarod, the recorder, the duduk, and the tabor.</p> <p>Please note that the venue is accessible only by stairs.</p> <p>Doors open: 2:30 p.m.</p> <p>Musicians: Ran Wang, guzheng | Annette Bauer, sarod, recorders, duduk, tabor</p> \",\"location\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"name\":\"Église Saint-Édouard\",\"address\":{\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\"streetAddress\":\"6500 Rue de Saint-Vallier, Montréal, QC H2S 2P7\"}}]}\n\t\t\t\tsun29mar15 h 00 minCarnets de soie : Échos d’est en ouest15 h 00 min(GMT-04:00) Église Saint-Édouard\n    Event DetailsCome and experience this musical performance that journeys along the Silk Road from East to West.\nIn their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang and Annette Bauer travel the Silk Road, from    \n        \n            Event Details\n            \n                Come and experience this musical performance that journeys along the Silk Road from East to West.\nIn their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang and Annette Bauer travel the Silk Road, from China to Italy via India. Their journey weaves together the music of the ancient Han Dynasty with that of the European Renaissance in a dialogue between their instruments: the guzheng, the sarod, the recorder, the duduk, and the tabor.\nPlease note that the venue is accessible only by stairs.\nDoors open: 2:30 p.m.\nMusicians: Ran Wang, guzheng | Annette Bauer, sarod, recorders, duduk, tabor\n            \n                    \n    \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tLearn More\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tLocationÉglise Saint-Édouard6500 Rue de Saint-Vallier, Montréal, QC H2S 2P7Other Events\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t \t\n\t\t \t\t\n\t\t \t\t\n\t\t \t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t"
      }
    ]
