  {
    "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/windborne/event_39718_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/windborne/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Red-Bold-Modern-Music-Event-Announcement-Instagram-Post-695-x-380-px.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g2740380"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/windborne/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Intimate concert | Windborne"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>“The most exciting vocal group of its generation”</strong></p> <p>Windborne&#8217;s captivating show draws on the singers&#8217; deep roots in vocal harmony traditions, while the absolute uniqueness of their artistic approach brings old songs into the present. Known for the innovation of their arrangements, their harmonies are bold and anything but predictable.</p> <p>With 20 years of experience studying polyphonic music around the world, Lauren Breunig, Jeremy Carter-Gordon, Lynn Rowan and Will Rowan share a vibrant energy on stage, with a blend of voices that could only come from decades of friendship and diligent practice. The ensemble moves effortlessly from one style of music to another, taking the audience on a journey that spans continents and centuries, illuminating and expanding the profound power and variety of the human voice. Singers educate while entertaining, sharing stories about their songs and explaining the context and characteristics of the styles in which they sing.</p> "
