    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                Deo Munyakazi is a renowned Rwandan musician, famous for his mastery of the inanga, a traditional harp from the African Great Lakes region. This essential instrument in Rwandan music is used to tell stories and pass on cultural values.\nDeo is committed to preserving this heritage while modernizing it. His performances, both technical and sensitive, captivate audiences, reflecting the unknown beauty of Rwandan culture. As a musical ambassador, he values oral traditions while building bridges with other styles.\nAn unmissable artist for discovering the rich soundscape of Rwanda through the presentation of new traditional melodies by Deo.\n            "
