    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Uuriintuya Khalivan - Morinkhuur from Mongolia"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Discover the fascinating beauty of the <b>morinkhuur</b>, the traditional horse-head fiddle, in the hands of Uuriintuya Khalivan, a young virtuoso from Inner Mongolia. Born into an ancient tradition, Uurintuya received her first instrument at the age of 12, a gift from her poet father.</p> <p>With her subtle playing of harmonics, the <b>morinkhuur</b> evokes the wild nature: the breath of the wind, the gallop of horses, the vastness of the steppe, and the whisper of spirits, with each note weaving a deep connection between humans and their environment.</p> <p>Let yourself be transported by the breath of this millennial music, where tradition and emotion become one. An unforgettable evening to connect with the vast Mongolian landscapes.</p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
