      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                From improvisation to co-composition, the Perse-Inca Duo draws on a variety of traditional rhythms and genres, bringing together Middle Eastern modal textures and Andean pentatonics, as well as Eastern melodies and Western harmonies.\nWith Federico Tarazona, composition, charango and Showan Tavakol, composition, kamancheh.\nThree 30-minute concerts:\n11 a.m., 12 p.m. and 1 p.m.\n            "
