    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Silk Diaries - From Persia to Mongolia - Amal&#039;Gamme"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>On the musical paths leading to the Silk Road, <strong>Uuriintuya Khalivan</strong>, carrying the breath of Mongolia, and <strong>Sadaf Amini</strong>, carrying the echoes of Iran, met in Montreal. Together, they chart their own course, where each note becomes a pause on the path to discovering the Other. They celebrate the richness of their respective cultures, woven like silk threads, seeking harmonies beyond borders, beyond distances.</p> <p>With the morin khuur (horsehead fiddle) and the santur (table zither), they create melodies that intertwine like the paths that crisscross the desert and the steppe. Their music resonates like an echo of centuries past, a testament to beauty and diversity, a vibrant tribute to the timeless magic of the Silk Road.</p> "
      }
    ],
