      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/kayhan-kalhor-erdal-erzincan-2/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kayhan Kalhor &amp; Erdal Erzincan"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div class='tuxCmsEdit__webEventSelection--subtitle'>Master Concert</div> <div class='tuxCmsEdit__webEventSelection--category'>In this rare meeting of musical masters, two of the world&#8217;s foremost exponents of ancient traditions converge to reveal a repertoire of exceptional beauty and depth.</div> <div class='tuxCmsEdit__webEventSelection--description'> <p>Iranian kamancheh virtuoso <strong>Kayhan Kalhor</strong> and Anatolian baglama luminary <strong>Erdal Erzincan</strong> have been performing together for over a decade, first capturing their musical dialogue in the acclaimed 2004 recording <em>The Wind</em>. Since then, they have refined their collaboration into a singular musical language, intricate yet expansive, rooted in tradition yet alive with contemporary vitality.</p> <p>Their interplay embodies an unspoken understanding; an artistry that transcends technique and invites audiences into a realm where music dissolves boundaries and speaks directly to the human spirit.</p> <p>Artists:<br /> Kayhan Kalhor – Kamancheh<br /> Erdal Erzincan – Baglama</p> <p>This event is made possible thanks to the support of our partners, the Canada Council for the Arts, the Conseil des arts et des lettres du Québec, the Conseil des arts de Montréal, and its sponsor Matin Tireh Dast, financial advisor.</p> <p><em>Parking is available behind the Musicians&#8217; Center, with entrance on Bullion Street.</em><br /> <em>Reserve your parking spot with <a href='https://clicknpark.com/get-clicknpark-app'>Clicknpark</a>.</em></p> </div> "
      }
    ],
