  {
    "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/cajon-workshop-bossa-nova/event_46500_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/cajon-workshop-bossa-nova/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Atelier-cajon-bossa.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g5397380"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/organizer": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g5397420"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://centredesmusiciensdumonde.com/en/calendrier/cajon-workshop-bossa-nova/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Cajón workshop - Bossa-nova"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>A versatile instrument par excellence, the <strong>cajón</strong> can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.</p> <p>This winter, join us for a series of intensive <strong>cajón workshops</strong> specially designed to teach you <strong>how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón</strong>.<br /> In three 1.5-hour sessions, you will learn to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of <strong>bossa nova</strong>.</p> <p>We will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.</p> <p>Thursdays, January 15, 22, and 29.</p> <p><em>Upcoming workshops: </em><br /> <em>Spanish rumba: February 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</em><br /> <em>Funk-pop: March 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</em></p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-1-15T18:00-4::00"
