    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>A versatile instrument par excellence, the <strong>cajón</strong> can provide a solid rhythmic foundation in a multitude of contexts: it adapts easily to almost any musical style.</p> <p>This winter, join us for a series of intensive <strong>cajón workshops</strong> specially designed to teach you <strong>how to accompany different musical styles on the cajón</strong>.<br /> In three 1.5-hour sessions, you will learn to recognize, understand, and play the essential rhythms of <strong>Spanish rumba</strong>.</p> <p>We will work with audio tracks to help you clearly perceive how your cajón playing fits into the musical ensemble.</p> <p>Wednesdays, February 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</p> <p><em>Upcoming workshops: </em><br /> <em>Funk-pop: March 11, 18, 25, from 6:00 p.m. to 7:30 p.m.</em></p> "
      }
