    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Echoes of Sakartvelo - Georgian Polyphonies"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                SOLD OUT\nGeorgian polyphony is one of the oldest and most complex of singing traditions. Family singing plays an essential role, having enabled it to survive through centuries of invasions and occupations.\nFor Ori Shlava (Shalva Makharashvili, Andrea Kuzmich and their sons Shalva-Lucas and Gabo), singing is as natural as breathing, rooted in family celebrations rather than stage performances.\nThe authenticity of their music stems from years of dedication and a musical heritage handed down from generation to generation.\nArtists :\nShalva Makharashvili : singer\nAndrea Kuzmich : singer\nShalva-Lucas : singer\nGabo : singer\n            "
      }
    ],
