    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Masmoudi Quartette in Saskatoon"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                When cultures meet in the music of the Masmoudi Quartet, the result is truly extraordinary. Jazz is enriched by the interaction between Western and Middle Eastern instruments to create a tapestry of sound that is both familiar and unexpected. The group’s leader, Mohamed Masmoudi, is originally from Tunisia, and his music incorporates influences from a life devoted to study, travel, and performance. His works are known for their melodic richness and multifaceted texture. A sample of Masmoudi’s repertoire is a journey through moods and landscapes, from the lively Labyrinth to the sensual Moorish Tango.\nAudiences will be intrigued by this unique mosaic of classical, jazz, and world music.\nArtists:\nMohamed Masmoudi: oud\nGuillame Martineau: piano\nGabriel Paquin-Buki: clarinet\nRémi-Jean Leblanc: double bass.\nPresented by the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra and the Saskatoon Jazz Society.\n            "
      }
    ],
