    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Come and enjoy the end-of-session concert by the <strong>Turkish folk choir</strong> directed by <strong>Sema Gultekin</strong>!</div> <div></div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Discover the rich world of <strong>traditional Turkish songs</strong> from different regions of <strong>Anatolia</strong>.<br /> Passed down orally from generation to generation, these songs evoke love, nature, and memorable moments in everyday life.<br /> Throughout the winter session, the choir explored this repertoire in an educational, warm, and sharing-oriented approach, respecting the regional and stylistic characteristics of this music.</div> <div></div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>April 1, 2026, 7 pm (doors open at 6:30 p.m.)</div> <div></div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'>Centre des musiciens du monde, 5043 Saint-Dominique Street, studio 201 upstairs, access via the Presbytère Saint-Enfant-Jésus in Mile End.</div> <div></div> <div class='x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak x1vvkbs xtlvy1s'><em>Each ticket sold helps support the activities of the Centre and its music school.</em></div> "
      }
    ],
