    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Concert - Turkish folk choir"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                Come and enjoy the end-of-session concert by the Turkish folk choir directed by Sema Gultekin!\n\nDiscover the rich world of traditional Turkish songs from different regions of Anatolia.\nPassed down orally from generation to generation, these songs evoke love, nature, and memorable moments in everyday life.\nThroughout the winter session, the choir explored this repertoire in an educational, warm, and sharing-oriented approach, respecting the regional and stylistic characteristics of this music.\n\nApril 1, 2026, 7 pm (doors open at 6:30 p.m.)\n\nCentre des musiciens du monde, 5043 Saint-Dominique Street, studio 201 upstairs, access via the Presbytère Saint-Enfant-Jésus in Mile End.\n\nEach ticket sold helps support the activities of the Centre and its music school.\n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
