    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carnets de soie : Échos d’est en ouest"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Come and experience this musical performance that journeys along the Silk Road from East to West.</p> <p>In their musical encounter, musicians Ran Wang and Annette Bauer travel the Silk Road, from China to Italy via India. Their journey weaves together the music of the ancient Han Dynasty with that of the European Renaissance in a dialogue between their instruments: the guzheng, the sarod, the recorder, the duduk, and the tabor.</p> <p>Please note that the venue is accessible only by stairs.</p> <p>Doors open: 2:30 p.m.</p> <p>Musicians: Ran Wang, guzheng | Annette Bauer, sarod, recorders, duduk, tabor</p> "
      }
    ],
